\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dlr, won rally on Greek deal;  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  caps\b0\par\par\uc2 1,219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2011\par 04:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Sing dlr at record on models, leveraged names; MAS spotted\par \par \uc2 * S.Korea estimated to have bought $500 mln-$1 bln to defend 1,050/dlr\par \par \uc2 * Ringgit up on lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Updates text, prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, July 22 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar rose to a new record and the South Korean won hit a near three-year peak on Friday as a European package to rescue Greece led investors to buy emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Asian authorities and technical signs being overbought.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, euro zone leaders agreed on a second rescue package for Greece, alleviated worries about contagion risks, which have put a brake on the regions \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Investors say they are waiting to see if U.S. politicians cobble together an agreement to avoid default, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to keep their bullish trend, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 If Washington fails to reach an agreement before the Aug. 2 deadline, that may dampen risk appetite again, but that will also push down the dollar, which will eventually support the regional units, some added.\par \par \uc2 "With EUR risk in the background at least in the near term, speculative players are back looking to go short USD/Asia pairs. Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have broken fresh highs... I think it continues to push emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher," said \uc2 Westpac\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Jonathan Cavenagh in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose for the week as concerns over the debt crisis in the two developed markets eased.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso and the Malaysian ringgit were the best performers during the week, gaining 1.3 percent and 1.1 percent, according to Reuters calculations.\par \par \uc2 Technically, some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  look overbought and some dealers and analysts said there could be a correction if the U.S. politicians fail to agree a debt deal.\par \par \uc2 "Every Asian country is long U.S. assets and if U.S. get downgraded, that will be a mayhem," said a Kuala Lumpur-based dealer.\par \par \uc2 The 14-day Relative Strength Index (RSI) for the USD/THB hit a three-month low of 28, suggesting the pair is headed higher in the short-term, and the baht could weaken from current levels.\par \par \uc2 The RSI of the Singapore dollar and Korean won are also hovering around the threshold of 30, indicating weakness ahead for the Asian units.\par \par \uc2 Central banks of Philippines, Singapore, Taiwan and Thailand were spotted buying greenbacks, dealers said. South Korean authorities were also spotted buying dollars, they added.\par \par \uc2 Market players expect the regional policymakers to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow their gains.\par \par \uc2 "The pace of appreciation is too strong and the swing is not driven by fundamentals," said Saktiandi Supaat, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Research at Maybank in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Model funds, leveraged names and proprietary accounts pushed up the Singapore dollar to a record high of 1.2086 per the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, agent banks had been spotted buying the U.S. dollars at 1.2100 but lowering the bids to 1.2090 in heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.\par \par \uc2 But the city-state \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to break through 1.20 level eventually as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised inflation forecast on Thursday and on views that the country would allow gradual appreciation.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 Seoul's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the won weaker than 1,050 per dollar, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier rose to 1,050.0, the highest since late August 2008, on demand from offshore real money funds and exporters.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors also turned to net buyers of local stocks\par \par \uc2 , ending an eight-session selling spree.\par \par \uc2 As the won threatened to break the level, the authorities stepped in the market and pushed it weaker minutes before the local market ended, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers speculated authorities had bought $500 million-$1 billion against the won.\par \par \uc2 Still, the authorities are unlikely to keep defending certain levels, given the country's fight against inflation, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "Today they showed strong determination to defend 1,050. But it does not mean 'don't touch the level ever'," said a foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 "Today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggest 'don't touch the level in a single day," he added.\par \par \uc2 If dollar/won breaches 1,050, it may head to 1,046, around a falling trend line which starts from November last year.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The baht rose on strong demand from proprietary accounts and leveraged funds.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying dollars from 29.84 per dollar level all the way down, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been pressured by the country's politics, has outperformed its Asian peers since the July 3 general election outcome eased political uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  saw short-term corrections in the baht, saying its recent gains are seen excessive and advised investors to position for it.\par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow down the baht's appreciation and \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade balance is likely to turn to deficit more often on strong oil prices, \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "We recommend positioning for a near-term reversal of recent THB gains by buying the 1m USD/THB forward at 29.94/USD, targeting 30.35/USD," it said in a note.\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 The ringgit gained on heavy demand from proprietary accounts, model funds and exporters.\par \par \uc2 Some covered dollar-short positions taking profits, but a lack of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  provided more support to the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0720 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par Japan yen        78.61          78.30       -0.39\par Sing dlr        1.2085         1.2104       +0.16\par Taiwan dlr      28.815         28.890       +0.26\par Korean won     1051.70        1054.60       +0.28\par Baht             29.78          29.91       +0.44\par Peso             42.40          42.62       +0.52\par Rupiah         8525.00        8529.00       +0.05\par Rupee            44.37          44.50    