\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For April 26\b0\par\par\uc2 2,540 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2011\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIA OUTPUT GROWTH MAY BE CUT BY UP TO 1.5 PERCENTAGE POINTS IN 2011 - ADB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Asian Development Bank warned Tuesday that Asian output growth could be cut by up to 1.5 percentage points if recent global food and oil price rises persist for the rest of the year, with the soaring cost of food threatening to push millions of people in the region into "extreme poverty." (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LEE KUAN YEW: US POLICIES BAD FOR DOLLAR; SINGAPORE SEEKS BALANCE ON STRONGER LOCAL DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Former Singapore Prime Minister Lee Kuan Yew said a stronger local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could help ease inflation in the fast-growing Asian city-state, even as he warned of a continued weak U.S. dollar--and potentially more inflation--in the U.S. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA REITERATES 11.50% MINIMUM CAPITAL ADEQUACY RATIO FOR TOP 5 BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's banking regulator Tuesday reiterated that the country's five largest banks must keep a minimum capital adequacy ratio of 11.50%, and said banks should improve their capital management over time. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA MAY TIGHTEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RULES FURTHER THAN EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government said Tuesday it may tighten rules on banks' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions further than expected, in a strengthened effort to shore up the financial system and help shield the economy from speculative \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flows. (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA BANKS MAY TAKE ON KRW400BLN IN REAL ESTATE LOANS - FSS OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's 18 domestic commercial banks are looking at taking on a combined KRW400 billion in real-estate project financing loans held by the troubled savings bank sector, a senior official at the local financial watchdog said Tuesday. (published 0251 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: HIGH YIELD SUPPORTS TWO-YEAR JGB AUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An auction of two-year Japanese government bonds met stronger-than-expected demand Tuesday as the deal remained attractive for yield-hungry investors. (published 0510 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN METI: MOST MANUFACTURERS EXPECT NORMAL MATERIALS SUPPLY BY OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry said Tuesday that more than 70% of earthquake-hit manufacturers expect their supplies of raw materials and parts to normalize by October. (published 0538 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN AUTO ASSOCIATION HEAD: HARD TO MAKE THIS FY OUTPUT PLANS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese automakers are having difficulty fixing their production plans for the current fiscal year as they are still trying to bring output back to normal after the earthquake on March 11, the chairman of the Japan Automobile Manufacturers Association said Tuesday. (published 0541 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA PBOC OFFICIAL: TO EXPAND YUAN TRADE SETTLEMENT TO WHOLE NATION IN 2011 - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will expand a cross-border yuan trade settlement trial to the whole nation this year, the Securities Times reported Tuesday on its website, citing Li Bo, head of the second monetary policy department of the People's Bank of China. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: SINGAPORE MARCH MANUFACTURING OUTPUT GROWS 22% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's manufacturing output rebounded in March thanks to the volatile pharmaceuticals sector lifting local output while factory production in the Asian region gathered steam. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANK OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 THAILAND\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : HAVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET TO CURB BAHT'S RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market "at times" to curb the baht's rise, but such moves have only been to try and limit short-term volatility, Gov. Prasarn Trairatvorakul said Tuesday. (published 0352 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : INTEREST RATE CYCLE REMAINS ON UPTREND DUE TO INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The interest rate cycle remains on an uptrend because of continuing inflationary pressures, Bank of Thailand Assistant Gov. Pongpen Ruengvirayudh said Tuesday. (published 0328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : CORE INFLATION COULD REACH UPPER END OF TARGET RANGE IN 4TH QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's core inflation could reach the upper end of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target range in the fourth quarter, Bank of Thailand Assistant Gov. Pongpen Ruengvirayudh said Tuesday. (published 0348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA SCRAPS DUTIES TO HELP BOOST TEXTILE, FILM, SHIPPING SECTORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia has scrapped import duties for certain types of machinery, goods and vessels to spur the competitiveness of its shipping, textile and film industries, according to a document seen by Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW ZEALAND GOVERNMENT TO POSTPONE INTRODUCTION OF NEW FUEL TAX \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand government has postponed the introduction of a new fuel tax due to the weakness of the country's economy, Transport Minister Steven Joyce said Tuesday. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 AGRICULTURAL BANK OF CHINA\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO SELL CNY30 BLN BONDS IN NEAR TERM - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Agricultural Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to sell CNY30 billion worth of subordinated bonds on the interbank market in the near term to boost its capital, a person familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0505 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDONESIA PLANS TO SELL $1.5B GLOBAL BOND TO YIELD IN 'LOW 5% AREA' - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Republic of Indonesia plans to raise $1.5 billion through the sale of a 10-year global dollar bond, which will conclude Wednesday, a person familiar with the proposed deal said Tuesday. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ WATCH: BOJ LIKELY TO CUT GROWTH FORECAST ON QUAKE IMPACT, KEEP RATES STEADY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan is expected to slash its growth forecast for the current fiscal year due to a "supply shock" caused by the March 11 earthquake, but will likely hold off on taking additional easing action for now. (published 0341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: NEW ZEALAND \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LIKELY TO HOLD CASH RATE AT 2.50% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand is expected to hold the Official Cash Rate at 2.50% Thursday, after cutting the rate last month to counter the effects of a 6.3-magnitude earthquake that devastated New Zealand's second-largest city of Christchurch. (published 0239 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MINMETALS RESOURCES WITHDRAWS OFFER TO ACQUIRE EQUINOX MINERALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Minmetals Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday it has decided not to pursue its C$6.3 billion takeover bid for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Equinox Minerals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: NINTENDO PRESIDENT LAMENTS "WEAKER THAN EXPECTED" 3DS SALES IN US, EUROPE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The president of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nintendo Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that sales of the new 3DS handheld game machine have been disappointing, not only in Japan, where the March 11 earthquake hurt consumer sentiment, but also in the U.S. and Europe. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CAPITALAND 1Q NET PROFIT MORE THAN TRIPLES TO S$101.5M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore property developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 CapitaLand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday its first-quarter net profit more than tripled from a year earlier on higher contributions from Singapore, China and Australia projects, but the result also reflects changes to the group's accounting policy. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PERENNIAL CHINA RETAIL TRUST SETS SINGAPORE IPO PRICE RANGE AT S$0.70-S$0.76/UNIT - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Perennial China Retail Trust has set an indicative price range for its revived Singapore initial public offering at S$0.70 to S$0.76 per unit in a transaction that could raise up to S$840 million, a person familiar with the situation said Tuesday. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SONY: PLAN TO LAUNCH TWO TABLET COMPUTERS LATER THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A year after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . launched the iPad, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sony Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it plans to enter the tablet computer segment later this year with two models running \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Android operating system. (published 0552 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STX OFFSHORE SIGNS LOI TO BUILD CONTAINER SHIPS WORTH ABOUT KRW3T - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 STX Offshore & Shipbuilding Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has signed a letter of intent to build more than 20 container ships worth about KRW3 trillion for Canada-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Seaspan Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a person familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0129 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NISSAN: APRIL DOMESTIC OUTPUT EXPECTED ABOVE 40% OF YR-EARLIER LEVEL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nissan Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that its domestic production in April will be just above 40% of the actual volume of a year earlier, but it aims to lift the rate to more than 50% and to produce more vehicles in the following month. (published 0645 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIAN GOVERNMENT: TO ASK TELKOM TO PUT ASIDE 55% OF 2010 NET PROFIT FOR DIVIDEND PAYMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian government will ask \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Telekomunikasi Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  to put aside 55% of its 2010 net profit for dividend payment, an official at the state-enterprise ministry told reporters Tuesday. (published 0642 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CANON POSTS 1Q PROFIT DECLINE, WARNS ON "EXTREMELY UNCERTAIN" OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canon Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Tuesday reported a decline in net profit for the fiscal first quarter, issued a profit warning for the full fiscal year and said its business outlook is "extremely uncertain" due to the impact of the March 11 earthquake. (published 0648 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 HAITONG SECURITIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  PLANS INITIAL SHARE SALE IN HONG KONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Haitong Securities Co. Tuesday became the second mainland-listed Chinese brokerage in nearly two months to seek a stock listing in Hong Kong, as it seeks to expand its international presence and tap into Beijing's long-term goal of globalizing the yuan. (published 0621 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COMPAL ELECTRONICS 1ST-QUARTER NET PROFIT NT$3.49 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Compal Electronics Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday its first-quarter net profit fell sharply from a year earlier. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GUINNESS PEAT\f28 \uc2 \f2 : COATS UNIT TO APPEAL EUR110.25 MLN FINE IN MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 26-04-11 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. thread maker Coats Holdings Ltd. will appeal a EUR110.25 million fine relating to an alleged market-sharing agreement next month, parent company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Guinness Peat Group PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 2317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DAIWA SECURITIES JAN-MAR NET LOSS WIDENS TO Y33.13 BILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daiwa Securities Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday its net loss in the January-March period widened from a year earlier, with trading \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hurt by the post-earthquake market instability and ongoing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility. (published 0635 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SIME DARBY\f28 \uc2 \f2  UNIT GETS MYR1.15 BLN FABRICATION CONTRACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sime Darby Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s unit Sime Darby Engineering Sdn. Bhd. has received a MYR1.15 billion contract to construct topside facilities for the Kebabangan Northern Hub Development project off the coast of Malaysian Borneo state of Sabah. (published 0023 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE BOURSE TO REVISE CRITERIA FOR CONSTITUENTS OF STOCK INDEXES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine Stock Exchange, operator of the country's stock market, said Tuesday it will revise in September the criteria that determine the constituents of its various stock indexes, including its bellwether PSEi. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AIRASIA CARRIED 4.32 MLN PASSENGERS IN 1Q, UP 17% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AirAsia Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Southeast Asia's largest budget airline by fleet, said Tuesday it carried 17% more passengers in the first quarter compared with a year earlier. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BELLE INTERNATIONAL: CHAIRMAN HOSPITALIZED; CEO TO BECOME ACTING CHAIRMAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Belle International Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its Chairman Tang Yiu has suffered a stroke and has been hospitalized. (published 0030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINOPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2 : GUANGDONG UNIT VIOLATED COMPANY'S RULES; PUNISHED EMPLOYEES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Petroleum & Chemical Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its Guangdong subsidiary's purchases of expensive spirits violated Sinopec's corporate rules, adding it has punished employees responsible for the purchases, including the unit's former general manager, Lu Guangyu. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASTRA AGRO 1Q NET PROFIT IDR682.23 BLN VS 284.209 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Astra Agro Lestari\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported Tuesday its first quarter net profit jumped to IDR682.23 billion from IDR284.209 billion a year earlier. (published 0628 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE BOURSE SUSPENDS ALLIANCE FOODS SHARE TRADING ON PENDING ACQUISITION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine Stock Exchange on Tuesday suspended \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alliance Select Foods International Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s shares from trading as it is awaiting more details of a pending acquisition by the company's unit in the U.S. (published 0127 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SM DEVELOPMENT PLANS PHP17 BLN CAPITAL EXPENDITURE IN 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine property developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 SM Development Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said it plans to spend PHP17 billion to launch up to five new residential high-rise projects this year. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES FALL; TOKYO HIT BY WEAK EARNINGS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were down Tuesday, with Tokyo hurt by weak earnings reports from the likes of Nintendo and worries about the impact of last month's natural disasters on corporate Japan. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN TO SEND IN ROBOTS TO EXAMINE REACTOR AS TEPCO READIES WATER FILLING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese authorities were preparing Tuesday to deploy a pair of U.S.-made robots to examine the containment vessel of Reactor No. 1 at the quake-hit Fukushima Daiichi nuclear complex. Meanwhile, the plant operator was preparing to fill the vessel with water to prevent the spent fuel from overheating. (published 0405 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW ZEALAND GOVERNMENT TO POSTPONE INTRODUCTION OF NEW FUEL TAX \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand government has postponed the introduction of a new fuel tax due to the weakness of the country's economy, Transport Minister Steven Joyce said Tuesday. (published 0415 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ITOCHU TO STUDY FEASIBILITY OF LNG PROJECT WITH \f28 \uc2 \f2 GAZPROM\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Itochu Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that a Japanese consortium led by the trading house will study feasibility of a liquefied natural gas project in eastern Russia with Russian gas firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 OAO Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0038 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JX: EXPECT TO RESTART QUAKE-HIT KASHIMA REFINERY BY END-JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JX Nippon Oil & Energy Corp., Japan's largest refiner by capacity, said Tuesday that it expects to restart the 252,500-barrel-a-day Kashima refinery northeast of Tokyo by the end of June. (published 0054 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA SEES REDUCED SUGAR OUTPUT, HIGH PRICES TO CONTINUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's sugar production will likely fall around 2.6% this marketing year, but demand, which is falling, will be "completely" met on the back of adequate sugar reserves and relatively affordable imports, according to China Sugar Association President Jia Zhiren and other government officials. (published 0447 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA TRADE INSURANCE TO SIGN MOU WITH \f28 \uc2 \f2 SAUDI ARAMCO\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Trade Insurance Corporation said Tuesday that it will sign a memorandum of understanding with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Saudi Arabian Oil Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Saudi Aramco\f28 \uc2 \f2  later in the day for cooperation in project financing. (published 0203 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MINMETALS RESOURCES WITHDRAWS OFFER TO ACQUIRE EQUINOX MINERALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Minmetals Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday it has decided not to pursue its C$6.3 billion takeover bid for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Equinox Minerals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0523 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASIA TANKER: TIGHT TONNAGE SUPPORTS CLEAN VESSELS; VLCCS LIKELY QUIET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia's clean petroleum product tanker market will likely continue to be mostly supported by tight tonnage, while rates for vessels shipping crude may see little change again for another week. (published 0330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US 2011-12 HARD WINTER WHEAT OUTPUT MAY FALL 26% -CONSILIAGRA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. hard winter wheat output may fall by as much as 26% to around 750 million bushels in the crop year that begins June 1, due to a severe drought in parts of the country's southwest, a senior industry analyst said. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA FOOD SECRETARY: MAY CONSIDER ALLOWING MORE SUGAR EXPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India may consider allowing more sugar exports under the open general licence program in addition to the 500,000 metric tons it approved last week, Food Secretary B.C Gupta said Tuesday. (published 0632 GMT) [ 26-04-11 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110426e74q000i9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
