\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 984 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2011\par 09:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIA OUTPUT GROWTH MAY BE CUT BY UP TO 1.5 PERCENTAGE POINTS IN 2011 - ADB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Asian Development Bank warned Tuesday that Asian output growth could be cut by up to 1.5 percentage points if recent global food and oil price rises persist for the rest of the year, with the soaring cost of food threatening to push millions of people in the region into "extreme poverty." (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par LEE KUAN YEW: US POLICIES BAD FOR DOLLAR; SINGAPORE SEEKS BALANCE ON STRONGER LOCAL DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Former Singapore Prime Minister Lee Kuan Yew said a stronger local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could help ease inflation in the fast-growing Asian city-state, even as he warned of a continued weak U.S. dollar--and potentially more inflation--in the U.S. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA REITERATES 11.50% MINIMUM CAPITAL ADEQUACY RATIO FOR TOP 5 BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's banking regulator Tuesday reiterated that the country's five largest banks must keep a minimum capital adequacy ratio of 11.50%, and said banks should improve their capital management over time. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA MAY TIGHTEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RULES FURTHER THAN EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government said Tuesday it may tighten rules on banks' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions further than expected, in a strengthened effort to shore up the financial system and help shield the economy from speculative \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flows. (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA BANKS MAY TAKE ON KRW400BLN IN REAL ESTATE LOANS - FSS OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's 18 domestic commercial banks are looking at taking on a combined KRW400 billion in real-estate project financing loans held by the troubled savings bank sector, a senior official at the local financial watchdog said Tuesday. (published 0251 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: HIGH YIELD SUPPORTS TWO-YEAR JGB AUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An auction of two-year Japanese government bonds met stronger-than-expected demand Tuesday as the deal remained attractive for yield-hungry investors. (published 0510 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN METI: MOST MANUFACTURERS EXPECT NORMAL MATERIALS SUPPLY BY OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry said Tuesday that more than 70% of earthquake-hit manufacturers expect their supplies of raw materials and parts to normalize by October. (published 0538 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN AUTO ASSOCIATION HEAD: HARD TO MAKE THIS FY OUTPUT PLANS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese automakers are having difficulty fixing their production plans for the current fiscal year as they are still trying to bring output back to normal after the earthquake on March 11, the chairman of the Japan Automobile Manufacturers Association said Tuesday. (published 0541 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC OFFICIAL: TO EXPAND YUAN TRADE SETTLEMENT TO WHOLE NATION IN 2011 - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will expand a cross-border yuan trade settlement trial to the whole nation this year, the Securities Times reported Tuesday on its website, citing Li Bo, head of the second monetary policy department of the People's Bank of China. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: SINGAPORE MARCH MANUFACTURING OUTPUT GROWS 22% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's manufacturing output rebounded in March thanks to the volatile pharmaceuticals sector lifting local output while factory production in the Asian region gathered steam. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANK OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 THAILAND\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : HAVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET TO CURB BAHT'S RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market "at times" to curb the baht's rise, but such moves have only been to try and limit short-term volatility, Gov. Prasarn Trairatvorakul said Tuesday. (published 0352 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : INTEREST RATE CYCLE REMAINS ON UPTREND DUE TO INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The interest rate cycle remains on an uptrend because of continuing inflationary pressures, Bank of Thailand Assistant Gov. Pongpen Ruengvirayudh said Tuesday. (published 0328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : CORE INFLATION COULD REACH UPPER END OF TARGET RANGE IN 4TH QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's core inflation could reach the upper end of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target range in the fourth quarter, Bank of Thailand Assistant Gov. Pongpen Ruengvirayudh said Tuesday. (published 0348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA SCRAPS DUTIES TO HELP BOOST TEXTILE, FILM, SHIPPING SECTORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia has scrapped import duties for certain types of machinery, goods and vessels to spur the competitiveness of its shipping, textile and film industries, according to a document seen by Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEW ZEALAND GOVERNMENT TO POSTPONE INTRODUCTION OF NEW FUEL TAX \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand government has postponed the introduction of a new fuel tax due to the weakness of the country's economy, Transport Minister Steven Joyce said Tuesday. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 AGRICULTURAL BANK OF CHINA\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO SELL CNY30 BLN BONDS IN NEAR TERM - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Agricultural Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to sell CNY30 billion worth of subordinated bonds on the interbank market in the near term to boost its capital, a person familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0505 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: INDONESIA PLANS TO SELL $1.5B GLOBAL BOND TO YIELD IN 'LOW 5% AREA' - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Republic of Indonesia plans to raise $1.5 billion through the sale of a 10-year global dollar bond, which will conclude Wednesday, a person familiar with the proposed deal said Tuesday. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par BOJ WATCH: BOJ LIKELY TO CUT GROWTH FORECAST ON QUAKE IMPACT, KEEP RATES STEADY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan is expected to slash its growth forecast for the current fiscal year due to a "supply shock" caused by the March 11 earthquake, but will likely hold off on taking additional easing action for now. (published 0341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: NEW ZEALAND \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LIKELY TO HOLD CASH RATE AT 2.50% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand is expected to hold the Official Cash Rate at 2.50% Thursday, after cutting the rate last month to counter the effects of a 6.3-magnitude earthquake that devastated New Zealand's second-largest city of Christchurch. (published 0239 GMT) [ 26-04-11 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110426e74q000ho\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
