\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2011\par 06:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIA OUTPUT GROWTH MAY BE CUT BY UP TO 1.5 PERCENTAGE POINTS IN 2011 - ADB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Asian Development Bank warned Tuesday that Asian output growth could be cut by up to 1.5 percentage points if recent global food and oil price rises persist for the rest of the year, with the soaring cost of food threatening to push millions of people in the region into "extreme poverty." (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA MAY TIGHTEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RULES FURTHER THAN EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government said Tuesday it may tighten rules on banks' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions further than expected, in a strengthened effort to shore up the financial system and help shield the economy from speculative \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flows. (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA BANKS MAY TAKE ON KRW400BLN IN REAL ESTATE LOANS - FSS OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's 18 domestic commercial banks are looking at taking on a combined KRW400 billion in real-estate project financing loans held by the troubled savings bank sector, a senior official at the local financial watchdog said Tuesday. (published 0251 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER REITERATES TAX OVERHAUL PLAN TO BE READY BY JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister said Tuesday the government still aims to draft a long-term plan by the end of June to overhaul the nation's strained tax and social security systems, even as officials appear preoccupied with dealing with the aftermath of a major earthquake. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANK OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 THAILAND\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : HAVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET TO CURB BAHT'S RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market "at times" to curb the baht's rise, but such moves have only been to try and limit short-term volatility, Gov. Prasarn Trairatvorakul said Tuesday. (published 0352 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : INTEREST RATE CYCLE REMAINS ON UPTREND DUE TO INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The interest rate cycle remains on an uptrend because of continuing inflationary pressures, Bank of Thailand Assistant Gov. Pongpen Ruengvirayudh said Tuesday. (published 0328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : CORE INFLATION COULD REACH UPPER END OF TARGET RANGE IN 4TH QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's core inflation could reach the upper end of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target range in the fourth quarter, Bank of Thailand Assistant Gov. Pongpen Ruengvirayudh said Tuesday. (published 0348 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA, TAIWAN BANKING REGULATORS TO MEET TWICE A YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The banking regulators of China and Taiwan said Monday their chiefs have agreed to meet twice a year to discuss the regulation of Taiwan banks in China and vice versa, while lower-level exchanges between the two will be conducted as often as needed. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA ISSUES PROPOSED INCOME TAX LAW REVISIONS FOR PUBLIC FEEDBACK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's legislature has issued the full text of its proposed individual income tax law revisions for public feedback until May 31, the National People's Congress said Monday. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: SPEAKER BOEHNER: LOWERING SUBSIDIES TO OIL FIRMS SHOULD BE 'LOOKED AT' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal government subsidies paid to big oil companies should be "looked at" as lawmakers strive to tackle federal budget deficits, House Speaker John Boehner said Monday. (published 0110 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: MIE HOLDINGS PLANS DEBUT GLOBAL DOLLAR BOND AFTER ROADSHOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MIE Holdings Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it plans to sell U.S. dollar-denominated bonds to finance acquisitions, repay debt as well as for working capital and general corporate purposes. (published 0128 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF SHANGHAI PLANS TO SELL UP TO CNY5 BLN BONDS IN NEAR TERM -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Shanghai\f28 \uc2 \f2  Co. plans to sell up to CNY5 billion worth of subordinated bonds on the interbank market in the near term to supplement its capital, a person familiar with the situation said Tuesday. (published 0134 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA PLANS TO SELL GLOBAL BOND TO YIELD IN 'LOW 5% AREA' TODAY OR TOMORROW - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Republic of Indonesia plans to sell a benchmark 10-year global dollar bond today or tomorrow to yield in the "low 5% area," a person familiar with the proposed deal said Tuesday. (published 0336 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par BOJ WATCH: BOJ LIKELY TO CUT GROWTH FORECAST ON QUAKE IMPACT, KEEP RATES STEADY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan is expected to slash its growth forecast for the current fiscal year due to a "suppl