\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand \highlight\uc2 : Have  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market To Curb Baht's Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2011\par 05:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quote in the 3rd paragraph, baht level in the 4th paragraph, quote in the 6th paragraph, asset price inflation risk in the 7th paragraph, factors affecting capital movement in the 8th paragraph, quote in the 9th paragraph, inflation risk in the 10th paragraph, inflation details in the 11th paragraph, impact from Thai-Cambodia tensions in the 12th paragraph)\par \par \uc2 By Phisanu Phromchanya\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market "at times" to curb the baht's rise, but such moves have only been to try and limit short-term volatility, Gov. Prasarn Trairatvorakul said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 He told a seminar that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market is not meant to resist market mechanisms.\par \par \uc2 "The BOT has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the (\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) market at times at various levels to limit short-term volatility of the baht, but we are not intending to reverse the major trend," said Prasarn.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  was suspected of stepping into the market several times last week, according to local dealers, as it attempted to slow the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. The dollar was trading at around THB29.98 to THB30.00 in morning trade Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Prasarn said that Thailand's relatively strong economic fundamentals, along with its continuous trade surplus, are attracting capital inflows, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely monitoring the market for speculative activity.\par \par \uc2 "The size of the international capital flows has increased significantly at present because of excess global liquidity as a result of extra-accommodative monetary policies by the U.S., the European Union and Japan to stimulate their economies," he said.\par \par \uc2 Massive capital inflows could cause asset price inflation while also increasing volatility risk in case of capital flight, he said.\par \par \uc2 Among factors affecting global capital movement are the fragility of the economic recovery in the Group of Three leading industrial nations, the euro zone public debt problem, geopolitical tension in the Middle East and Africa, natural disasters, and any adjustment of U.S. monetary policy, said Prasarn.\par \par \uc2 "It would be difficult to separate 'hot money' from other types of inflows, but we are closely monitoring them and so far the level is not considered worrisome," he said.\par \par \uc2 Inflation pressures are likely to remain in the second half due to high oil and consumer goods prices while the domestic economy will maintain its recovery momentum, he said.\par \par \uc2 Thailand's consumer price index rose 3.14% in March compared with the same month a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, he said any economic impact from renewed tension along the Thai-Cambodia border--which has seen several soldiers on both sides killed--will likely be limited as exports to Cambodia account for less than 1% of Thailand's total exports.\par \par \uc2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2690 4200; phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com [ 26-04-11 0352GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110426e74q00071\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
