\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, rupiah down on profit-taking before Fed\b0\par\par\uc2 1,082 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2011\par 04:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Won down 0.4 pct on tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  control worries\par \par \uc2 * Rupiah, peso down 0.3 pct on dlr short-cover before FOMC\par \par \uc2 * Baht eases on importers' end-month dlr demand\par \par \uc2 (Updates with text, prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, April 26 (Reuters) - The South Korean won and the Indonesian rupiah fell on Tuesday, leading declines in most regioanl \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors took profits on recent rallies and awaited comments from the Federal Reserve that could determine the short-term direction of the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could pull back further in near term as investors still hold dollar-short positions, but their overall bullish trend remain intact, dealers and analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Regional central banks are expected to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to slow gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but are unlikely to attempt to reverse their strength, they added.\par \par \uc2 "Fundamentally, we are bullish on AXJ \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the global recovery and widening US-AXJ rates spreads, which should drive capital inflows into the region," said Standard Chartered said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have seen healthy gains so far this year on inflows to the region's stocks and bonds, and on expectations of further policy tightening to contain inflation amid robust economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Standard Chartered said shorter-dated bonds in particular should benefit from \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -driven inflows. [ID:nL3E7FQ09D]\par \par \uc2 Investors are keeping an eye on the Fed's two-day meeting, which starts later in the day.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to say it will stick to its plan to complete a $600 billion bond-buying programme in June, with the focus on a post-meeting news conference by Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke -- the first regularly scheduled news briefing by a Fed chief in its 97-year history.\par \par \uc2 But the dollar is seen fragile as the Fed will be in no rush to unwind its super-easy monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won shed 0.5 percent against the dollar as offshore hedge funds and real money investors covered dollar-short positions.\par \par \uc2 Worries about possible tougher \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls also weighed on the won as the country started inspecting foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives trading by four banks, including branches of two foreign banks, that government sources have said could lead to reductions in ceilings of such positions.\par \par \uc2 After the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market closed, two government sources said the country will likely to trim the ceilings by at least one-fifth "as widely expected". [ID:nL3E7FQ0UO]\par \par \uc2 Still, the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  found support as exporters bought it for settlements, especially around 1,085 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "I don't see any other reasons to sell the won except position adjustments. The won may fall more on short-covering, but I don't think it will weaken past 1,090," said a local bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The rupiah fell and filled most of a gap as investors covered dollar-short positions, but later recovered some losses as further falls are seen as limited.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost up to 0.8 percent to 8,690 against the dollar, a notch 8,692, the session high of 8,692 on April 1, a day before it gapped up.\par \par \uc2 The dollar/rupiah's 14-day relative strength index rose to 38.974, the highest since February 3, indicating the pair got out of an oversold territory.\par \par \uc2 The RSI had been below 30 since February 7 by the previous session except two days, as investors chased it on expectations that the country will allow more appreciation to fight inflation.\par \par \uc2 Still, the rupiah's gains is seen slow on caution over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . IFR said local banks bought the pair on behalf of Bank Indonesia. [ID:nIFR8mdh5y]\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 The peso fell on fixing related dollar demand and dollar-short covers before the Fed's meeting.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  , however, found support around 43.34 per dollar, the 61.8 percent Fibonacci retracement level of its November-January weakening trend.\par \par \uc2 A European bank dealer in Manila said the peso is unlikely to move much, adding it will stay within recent range of 43.00-43.50.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been seen defending 43.00 while the peso has a 50 percent retracement level of March-April strengthening trend around 43.51.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The baht eased on end-month dollar demand from importers and investors covered dollar-short positions.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governor said the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  periodically in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to limit volatility over the short term, following the baht's gains. [ID:nB7E7FL04N]\par \par \uc2 But a Bangkok-based dealer said "the market still needs to sell on rallies (in dollar/baht)".\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0720 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        81.69          81.83       +0.17\par  Sing dlr        1.2363         1.2359       -0.03\par  Taiwan dlr      28.916         28.930       +0.05\par  Korean won     1085.10        1081.30       -0.35\par  Baht             29.98          29.91       -0.23\par  Peso             43.30          43.19       -0.27\par  Rupiah         8645.00        8620.00       -0.29\par  Rupee            44.58          44.48       -0.21\par  Ringgit         2.9930         2.9920       -0.03\par  Yuan            6.5265         6.5277       +0.02\par                                                                                                \par  Change so far in 2011                                                                     \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        81.69          81.15       -0.66\par  Sing dlr        1.2363         1.2820       +3.70\par  Taiwan dlr      28.916         30.368       +5.02\par  Korean won     1085.10        1134.80       +4.58\par  Baht             29.98          30.14       +0.53\par  Peso             43.30          43.84       +1.25\par  Rupiah         8645.00        9005.00       +4.16\par  Rupee            44.58          44.70       +0.28\par  Ringgit         2.9930         3.0820       +2.97\par  Yuan            6.5265         6.5897       +0.97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Reuters \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \