\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Asia Central Banks  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  Again As  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Extend Rally\b0\par\par\uc2 796 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2011\par 10:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds yuan central parity fixing in paragraph 4; details on BOK \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in paragraphs 7-8; updates levels in paragraphs 9-11)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Martin Vaughan and In-Soo Nam \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The dollar continued to sell off sharply in Asia Thursday, prompting central banks in South Korea and Malaysia to try to curb the surge in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to long-term highs by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second day running.\par \par \uc2 South Korean authorities also said they will inspect \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions at banks, focusing on activity in the overseas non-deliverable forward market. The move comes as heavy dollar selling by offshore players, largely via the NDF market, has pushed the Korean won to multi-month highs in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 China fixed the yuan at another record high against the dollar, setting the tone for Asian trading where sentiment was also given a boost by upbeat U.S. economic data and a strong earnings-driven rally on Wall Street.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  set the central parity rate Thursday at 6.5228, down from Wednesday's record low fixing of 6.5294.\par \par \uc2 Strategists said that in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets, central banks around the region are trying to smooth sudden market moves, but likely won't stand in the way of the broad appreciation trend in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Asian central banks and government officials have made it very clear that they're going to use \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fight inflation," said Stuart Oakley, head of emerging market trading at the \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2 . "They're allowing their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move faster than they have before, and China is leading the way on that."\par \par \uc2 Traders said the Bank of Korea bought dollars throughout the session first at KRW1,080.00, then at KRW1,079 and KRW1,078 to cushion the dollar's slide. The greenback sank early to as low as KRW1,078.30, but ended the trading day around KRW1,080.30.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used at least one foreign bank and one local bank to execute trades, traders said. The head of BOK's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market team declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\uc2  bought dollars at MYR3.0120, and then later at MYR3.0080 and MYR3.0070 as the dollar fell to 13-year lows against the ringgit, local traders said.\par \par \uc2 The actions came as the U.S. dollar took a beating across the board, falling against the euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  soared into rarely-seen territory. The Australian dollar hit a 29-year high of S$1.0771, while the U.S. dollar touched C$0.9482 against the Canadian Loonie, a level not seen since 2007.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar fell to a fresh record low against the Singapore dollar, which has paced the gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reaching a low early Thursday of S$1.2342.\par \par \uc2 Traders in \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  were on vigil against further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Thai authorities to weaken the baht, following suspected market activity Wednesday by the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Better-than-expected U.S. housing data overnight helped to spur risk appetite Thursday as Asian equity markets opened higher.\par \par \uc2 But the main thing pushing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher against the U.S. dollar remains the sense that the U.S. Federal Reserve is lagging the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and others in its willingness to tighten policy.\par \par \uc2 "We've had pretty clear signals from the majority on the [Fed's Federal Open market Committee] that they don't see any problem with keeping monetary conditions in the U.S. as loose as possible for as long as possible," said Cliff Tan, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, Asian central banks have been tightening since last year to try to blunt higher food and fuel prices, and the ECB lifted its key policy rate earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 A stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes exports more expensive abroad, and central banks in Asia's export-oriented economies have historically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soften the blow of a sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise.\par \par \uc2 Korea is brandishing various tools to curb gains in the won. It announced Thursday it would conduct "inspections" into non-deliverable forward trades at four banks. Offshore investors have taken short positions on the dollar in the forward market, pushing the won higher.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the inspections might perturb the banks, but authorities can do little concretely to limit NDF trades, which are done beyond the jurisdiction of Korean authorities.\par \par \uc2 -By Martin Vaughan and In-Soo Nam, Dow Jones Newswires; +65 6415 4033; martin.vaughan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Min-Jeong Lee in Seoul and Kwan-por Lee in Kuala Lumpur contributed to this article. [ 21-04-11 0832GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110421e74l000qw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
