\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Asia Central Banks  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  As US, France Press China On Yuan\b0\par\par\uc2 932 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 12:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- South Korea, Malaysia, \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -- China sets yuan at a record-high against the dollar\par \par \uc2 -- U.S and France press China to let yuan rise\par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the lead and paragraph 11, Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  size in paragraph 4, comments by Korea finance ministry official in paragraphs 5-6, updates \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  quotes.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Arran Scott and Jieun Shin \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--South Korea, Malaysia and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were seen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow the rise of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday, as China set the yuan at a record-high while the U.S. and France called for more exchange-rate flexibility--code for wanting Beijing to let its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise faster.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The developments highlighted both the reservations in Asian nations about the speed of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' rise and the urgency felt in the U.S. and Europe, where governments argue a stronger yuan is essential to reducing trade imbalances that threaten global economic stability.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia's large trade surpluses, a major source of economic growth for the region, has put strong pressure on the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rise, which authorities have resisted by selling their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets. The trade surplus of China, now the world's second-biggest economy, has soared while the U.S. has run a persistent deficit, an imbalance Washington blames in part on an artificially weak Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea apparently bought $1 billion for won, Seoul-based traders said, citing dollar purchases near KRW1,100 in early trading and additional buy orders at KRW1,095 in the afternoon. It was the first time since March 25 that the BOK was seen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea's Finance Ministry, which sets the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, is closely watching the won and will counter any one-sided moves but isn't targeting a particular level, said Kim Ik-joo, director general of the ministry's International Finance Bureau.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Capital is flowing into the local financial system with foreigners buying a lot of local shares as they focus more on positive factors. We are closely monitoring the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to make sure there aren't any rapid one-sided moves," Kim said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar ended trading at KRW1,096.7, down from KRW1,104.20 late Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , similarly, sold ringgit to slow its rise, two Kuala Lumpur dealers said, spotting dollar purchases by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at MYR3.0250. The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was at MYR3.0250 in late Asian trade, down from MYR3.0255 late Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Singapore, some traders said there was speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been in the market, but \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore couldn't immediately be confirmed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said banks known to be MAS agents bought U.S. dollars around S$1.2617 in the morning. But the Singapore dollar faced strong upward pressure throughout the trading session, with the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  falling to a record low of S$1.2592 late in the afternoon, down from S$1.2622 late Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of buying $100 million to $200 million around THB30.24-THB30.27, traders said. The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was last at THB30.25.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A record-high fixing for the yuan in the morning set a bullish tone for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set its dollar parity at CNY6.5564, the lowest ever and down from Wednesday's fixing of CNY6.5586.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan, which ended trading at CNY6.5485 to the dollar in the onshore spot market, has risen 4.2% against since June, when China effectively ended its two-year \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg and vowed to make the yuan more flexible. Other Asian central banks watch Beijing closely, and to varying degrees have also allowed their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rise against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China appeared to be under renewed pressure Thursday to move faster on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  front at an informal meeting of finance ministers and central bankers from the Group of 20 industrial and developing nations held in the former Chinese capital of Nanjing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner, in prepared remarks at the meeting, argued forcefully for flexible exchange rates, calling the mismatch between fixed and floating exchange rates "the most important problem to solve in the international monetary system today."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This asymmetry in exchange rate policies creates a lot of tension," Geithner said. "It magnifies upward pressure on those emerging market exchange rates that are allowed to move and where capital accounts are much more open. It intensifies inflation risk in those emerging economies with undervalued exchange rates. And, finally, it generates protectionist pressures."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Geithner didn't mention the yuan in his prepared remarks, but there is little doubt his message was aimed at least in part at China.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French President Nicolas Sarkozy said the global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  system in its current form has fueled growing global imbalances. The world needs to move toward a more flexible exchange rate regime, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Vice Premier Wang Qishan said Beijing will work with others toward "a more equitable global monetary system" but avoided any reference to the yuan's exchange rate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Arran Scott, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4042; arran.scott@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Kanga Kong in Seoul, Phisanu Phromchanya in Bangkok, Esther Fung in Beijing, Christopher Wong in Singapore, Elffie Chew in Kuala Lumpur, and Aaron Back, Nathalie Boschat, Jean Yung and Shen Hong in Nanjing contributed to this article. [ 31-03-11 1022GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110331e73v000yx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
