\par\par \b \uc2 MONEY MARKETS-Short Thai swaps hit new 2-1/2 year highs\b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 06:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, March 3 (Reuters) - Short-dated Thai interest rate swaps climbed to fresh 2-1/2 year highs on Thursday with yields set to rise more in coming weeks as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightens policy and on expected inflows into the local money market.\par \par \uc2 * One-year Thai IRS rose to 2.70 percent, their highest since December 2008. They have risen by about 90 basis points in slightly more than a month, pushing the spread between 10-year and one-year swaps to a five-month low of 170 bps.\par \par \uc2 * The flattening of the IRS curve over the past month has been mainly driven by a surge in front-end rates, which in turn has been triggered a washout of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap trades caused by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Along with a steady stream of hawkish comments from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said paying in swaps is also from "kimchi funds", or Thai funds investing in Korean assets.\par \par \uc2 * At its peak in 2009, about $14 billion, or 30 percent of the entire Korean debt market, was owned by these funds, but their share has dwindled in recent months due to narrowing rate differentials between the two economies and after Seoul slapped a 15 percent withholding tax on debt investments last year.\par \par \uc2 * A lot of these maturing investments will flow back into Thailand and exchanged into baht around the second half of the year and the improved dollar liquidity in the markets would push up the floating leg of the swap fixing which is a synthetic rate implied from \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, Credit Agricole strategists said.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  has also turned hawkish in recent months, raising its benchmark interest rate by a quarter point to 2.25 percent on Jan. 12 following a similar increase in December. Another quarter point increase is expected next week.\par \par \uc2 * Six-month Thai baht fixings have rebounded this week to 2.43 percent, holding well above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main policy rate of 2.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Sugita Katyal)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-MONEY (WRAPUP 1)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|J|RBN|SI|UKI|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110303e7330008e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
