\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso dips on tight dollar liquidity; baht eases\b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2010\par 08:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yuan flat; PBOC mid-point reflects dollar fall on Thursday\par \par \uc2 * Dollar well bid vs Thai baht ahead of U.S. jobs data\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Dec 3 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso fell on Friday as the dollar was buoyed by tight dollar liquidity and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 China's yuan was flat against the dollar after the People's Bank of China set a higher mid-point to reflect the dollar index's 0.5 percent fall the previous day.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the PBOC might let the dollar's performance guide the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movements in the near term, but in the long term, appreciation appears likely to continue as China needs to fight imported inflation.\par \par \uc2 Spot yuan was trading at 6.6600 versus the dollar, little changed from Thursday's close of 6.6613. [ID:nTOE6B202S]\par \par \uc2 The following reports below are from Reuters and IFR Markets.\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 The dollar jumped at the open against the Philippine peso and tight onshore dollar liquidity and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an intraday high near 43.95.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 Dollar/baht opened near 30.00 and the dollar found support. Weak bond market sentiment and market expectations for further \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 30.00 underpinned sentiment. Traders were also unwilling to add to short dollar positions ahead of U.S. jobs data later on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0556 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move                  \par   Japan yen        83.62          83.87       +0.30                  \par   Sing dlr        1.3080         1.3065       -0.11                  \par   Taiwan dlr      30.340         30.340       +0.00                  \par   Korean won     1137.90        1149.30       +1.00                  \par   Baht             30.02          29.99       -0.10                  \par   Peso             43.94          43.65       -0.66                  \par   Rupiah         9010.00        9013.00       +0.03                  \par   Rupee            45.10          45.13       +0.08                  \par   Ringgit         3.1440         3.1510       +0.22                  \par   Yuan            6.6586         6.6613       +0.04                  \par \tab \par  Change so far in 2010\tab \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move                  \par   Japan yen        83.62          92.90      +11.10                  \par   Sing dlr        1.3080         1.4053       +7.44                  \par   Taiwan dlr      30.340         32.030       +5.57                  \par   Korean won     1137.90        1164.50       +2.34                  \par   Baht             30.02          33.32      +10.99                  \par   Peso             43.94          46.20       +5.14                  \par   Rupiah         9010.00        9420.00       +4.55                  \par   Rupee            45.10          46.54       +3.19                  \par   Ringgit         3.1440         3.4220       +8.84                  \par   Yuan            6.6586         6.8270       +2.53                  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Masayuki Kitano in Singapore, Chen