*DJ  Bank Of Thailand: Yuan Asset Investment Limited By Chinese Government\par \par \uc2 24 Nov 2010 02:01 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Thailand: No Immediate Concerns Over Inflation\par \par \uc2 24 Nov 2010 02:02 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Thailand: Flood Impact On Inflation Just Temporary\par \par \uc2 24 Nov 2010 02:02 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Thailand: Core Inflation May Still Reach Upper-End Of Target Next Year\par \par \uc2 24 Nov 2010 02:03 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Thailand: Core Inflation Target Range 0.5%-3.0%\par \par \uc2 24 Nov 2010 02:09 EDT DJ  Bank Of Thailand: "Tobin Tax" Among Potential Policy Tools\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones Newswires)--The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  wants to equip itself with various policy tools to ensure economic stability without hindering growth prospects, with a tax on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions one potential tool, BOT Gov. Prasarn Trairatvorakul said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The best thing for us is to have a variety of policy tools and then be able to use a mixture of them in good proportion, hopefully with good timing too," Prasarn said in a group interview.\par \par \uc2 Referring to the tax on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions, known as a "Tobin Tax," he said, "in our tool kit, it's one of the components."\par \par \uc2 If needed, the Tobin Tax could be introduced by emergency decree, requiring approval only from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Cabinet, not the lengthy parliamentary process needed to draft legislation, Prasarn said.\par \par \uc2 With many countries in Asia facing similar problems from surging capital inflows, Prasarn said central bankers have talked of potential cooperation in curbing flows.\par \par \uc2 "If the situation called for it, if conditions called for it, there could be cooperation" among central banks to control inflows, he said.\par \par \uc2 -- By Phisanu Phromchanya; (662) 690 4200; phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 Corrected November 24, 2010 05:09 ET (10:09 GMT)\par \par \uc2 24 Nov 2010 05:07 EDT DJ  CORRECT: Bank Of Thailand: "Tobin Tax" Among Potential Tools\par \par \uc2 ("=UPDATE: Bank Of Thailand: "Tobin Tax" Among Potential Tools," at 0933 GMT, misstated the day of the week in the first paragraph. The error also appeared the story "Bank Of Thailand: "Tobin Tax" Among Potential Policy Tools" at 0709 GMT. The correct version follows:)\par \par \uc2 By Phisanu Phromchanya\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  wants to equip itself with various policy tools to ensure economic stability without hindering growth prospects, with a tax on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions one possibility, Governor Prasarn Trairatvorakul said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The best thing for us is to have a variety of policy tools and then be able to use a mixture of them in good proportion, hopefully with good timing too," Prasarn said in a group interview.\par \par \uc2 Referring to the tax on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions, known as a "Tobin Tax," he said, "in our tool kit, it's one of the components."\par \par \uc2 If needed, the Tobin Tax could be introduced by emergency decree, requiring approval only from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Cabinet, not the lengthy parliamentary process needed to draft legislation, Prasarn said.\par \par \uc2 "We'll have to weigh the effectiveness and the cost," he said. "Practically it's very challenging, particularly for a country like Thailand that has liberalized this far."\par \par \uc2 With many countries in Asia facing similar problems from surging capital inflows, Prasarn said central bankers have talked of potential cooperation.\par \par \uc2 "If the situation called for it, if conditions called for it, there could be cooperation" among central banks to control inflows, he said.\par \par \uc2 Given the bearish trend of the dollar and the U.S. economic outlook, the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  has been trimming the proportion of dollar assets in its reserves, and its reserve management team is seeking other types of assets that offer better yields and can cover the cost of the bank's liabilities, Prasarn said.\par \par \uc2 "That exercise has been started for sometime, not just by us but by everybody," the governor said.\par \par \uc2 The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to increase yuan-denominated assets in its foreign reserves, but Prasarn said the Chinese government allows only a limited amount of qualified investors to invest in yuan, also known as renminbi.\par \par \uc2 It depends on "how proactively, how fast the Chinese government wants the renminbi to play a role in the international market," he said. "There's no sign they intend to do it in the near future, but in the medium term, in the longer term, that may be possible."\par \par \uc2 Members of the BOT's Monetary Policy Committee have made clear that they want to raise interest rates from the current abnormally low level, but the timing is important and the committee will weigh all relevant factors, Prasarn said. He gave no hints about the direction of monetary policy at the upcoming meeting Dec. 1.\par \par \uc2 Thailand's policy interest rate of 1.75% is quite low by regional standards, Prasarn said. But he noted that with massive inflows of capital from the West, partly inspired by U.S. quantitative easing moves, any rate hike would attract even more money and would be "like giving out benefits to undeserved investors."\par \par \uc2 "The MPC will look at these matters. We tend to take into account many facets of economic information," Prasarn said.\par \par \uc2 Most economists expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to once again stand pat next week, as recent data show growth slowing, while the baht is still showing a firmer tone and inflation remains manageable.\par \par \uc2 The MPC kept rates on hold at its last meeting in October amid mounting worries over the baht's rapid rise, after hiking by 25 basis points in each of its two previous meetings.\par \par \uc2 Prasarn said he sees no immediate threat of surging prices but said core inflation may still reach the upper end of the BOT's 0.5%-3.0% target range sometime next year.\par \par \uc2 He said any impact on inflation from recent floods--the country's worst in decades--will likely last for only three or four months.\par \par \uc2 The BOT is always on alert for asset bubbles forming, but despite economic growth of 9.3% in the first nine months of the year and massive capital inflows, the bank doesn't see any yet, Prasarn said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently tightened restrictions on housing loans worth THB10 million or less, a move which it says was a cautionary signal to the market about potential bubbles.\par \par \uc2 Prasarn said Thailand's economy has grown above trend in the first three quarters of the year and he expects the growth rate in the fourth quarter and next year to fall bcak to the country's normal trend of 3%-5%.\par \par \uc2 With export growth slowing, domestic demand is expected to play a larger role in economic growth, he said.\par \par \uc2 -By Phisanu Phromchanya, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2690 4200; phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 24, 2010 05:07 ET (10:07 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020101124e6bo0029d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
