\par\par \b \uc2 MONEY MARKETS-Thai swap rates fall as bond selloff spooks\b0\par\par\uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2010\par 06:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Foreign selling in Thai bonds may trigger dollar shortage\par \par \uc2  * Swaps decline may slow if \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  adds dollars\par \par \uc2  * Korea swaps ease after interest rate increase\par \par \uc2  By Saikat Chatterjee\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Nov 16 (Reuters) - Thai one-year swap rates fell to a five-month low on Tuesday on growing fears that foreign investors dumping their local bonds would trigger a shortage of dollars so close to the year end.\par \par \uc2  Capital controls in Thailand and other Asian countries, have made offshore investors cautious on local markets. Foreign demand for Thai debt has cooled considerably since Bangkok reimposed a 15 percent withholding tax on offshore purchases on Oct. 13.\par \par \uc2  As foreigners liquidate their positions and switch to dollars from baht, traders were concerned a scramble for dollars might push down the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forwards market and further weigh on swaps, since the floating leg of such contracts are determined by forwards. <THBFIX>.\par \par \uc2  "Inflows have slowed to about 50 percent of what they used to be before the withholding taxes and people are taking profits on the long end fearing that liquidity would dry up before the year end," said a senior rates trader at a foreign bank in Bangkok.\par \par \uc2  One-year swap contracts dropped by two basis points (bps) to 1.34 percent -- its lowest in late June -- taking its fall by 11 bps since last Friday as offshore receiving in swaps also took out some paid positions by local banks.\par \par \uc2  Six month fixings were at 1.02 percent on Tuesday compared to 1.23 percent on Friday pressuring swap rates lower.\par \par \uc2  Other traders said these concerns were overblown, pointing to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forward baht commitment book which has grown in recent weeks indicating it was still a net supplier of dollars in the forward market.\par \par \uc2  They expect the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to alleviate the dollar funding shortage if the bond selling by foreigners intensifies, in sharp contrast to the Philippines's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which artificially engineered a dollar shortage in its market earlier this month to break the peso's rally.\par \par \uc2  Foreigners have sold a cumulative net 6 billion baht of bonds over the last week, latest data from the Thai bond market association showed and these selling pressures have exacerberated big price movements at a time when banks are winding down trading activities and client flows have slowed.\par \par \uc2  In the cash market, 10-year yields <#THBMK=> extended their rise by six bps to 3.80 percent and five year yields popped above the 3 percent level -- a first in nearly three months as profit taking continued on the belly and the far end of the curve.\par \par \uc2  In Seoul, swap rates eased after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased interest rates as widely expected by 25 bps, cooling speculation that the won's gains would draw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's attention away from inflationary pressures. [ID:nTOE6AF01X]\par \par \uc2  One-year contracts <KRWIRS> edged lower by three bps to 3.13 percent, moving further away from a three-month peak hit on Monday.\par \par \uc2  In dollar funding markets, three month dollar rates in Singapore fell to 0.29 percent from 0.29112 percent on Monday, suggesting that LIBOR might be fixed lower later in the day.  (Editing by Kevin Plumberg)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-MONEY (WRAPUP 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|J|PHD|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101116e6bg0009e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
