\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Thai MOF Ready To Support  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  In Managing Baht\b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2010\par 06:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds more comments from minister and background)\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Thailand's Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said Monday that the ministry is ready to support the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2 's actions in managing the baht's volatility.\par \par \uc2 He reiterated that a decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb the baht's pace of appreciation rests solely with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Korn said that the global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  situation will be among key issues to be discussed at the upcoming G-20 meeting in November, which could result in guidance on sustaining stability among global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He added that Japan's attempt to curb the rise of yen has proven to be ineffective because it did so alone.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a small country. The result (of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) won't be different," he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 He said a solution to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue needs the cooperation of various countries.\par \par \uc2 Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in mid-September, buying dollars against the yen for the first time in six years to stem the yen's rise after it hit a 15-year high against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The baht has risen more than 9% in the year-to-date against the dollar in the wake of fund inflows across Asia. The dollar was at THB30.16-THB30.18 early Monday, compared with THB30.20 late Friday.\par \par \uc2 -By Bangkok Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2 690 4200; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com [ 04-10-10 0446GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101004e6a40008b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
