\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 29\b0\par\par\uc2 2,212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2010\par 09:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: JAPAN TANKAN SHOWS SEPTEMBER IMPROVEMENT, BUT OUTLOOK DARKENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sentiment among Japan's big manufacturers picked up for the sixth straight quarter at a faster pace than expected, the Bank of Japan's September tankan survey showed Wednesday, but companies are turning more cautious in their outlook for the coming quarter due to the surging yen and increased uncertainty over the global economy. (published 0212 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: HSBC CHINA SEPTEMBER PMI RISES TO FIVE-MONTH HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The HSBC China Manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index, a gauge of nationwide manufacturing activity, rose to a five-month high in September, likely reassuring markets China isn't facing a rapid slowdown, but sharp increases in the input and output price subindexes may renew concerns about a buildup of inflationary pressures. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: RESERVE BANK OF AUSTRALIA'S BROADBENT EXPECTS HIGHER AUSTRALIA GROWTH IN 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's economy will see stronger growth in 2011 spurred on by China, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  board member Jillian Broadbent Wednesday ahead of a closely watched rate decision next week when the bank is expected to tighten policy in an effort to manage the country's surging economy. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA: SHOULD BALANCE INFLATION, EXTERNAL RISKS WHEN OPERATING MACRO POLICIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea authorities should weigh the risk of faster inflation and a softer recovery in the global economy when implementing macroeconomic policies, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Wednesday. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: S KOREA AUGUST CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS FALLS; TO BEAT 2010 TARGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea ran its smallest current-account surplus in four months in August as trade gains shrank due to summer holidays, but the country is expected to chalk up a surplus for the full year that will easily surpass the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's $21 billion estimate. (published 0207 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NZ EXPORTS WEAKEN, REDUCING SUPPORT FOR RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's goods trade balance recorded a deficit in August after exports came in weaker than expected, stoking concerns over the strength of the country's economic recovery. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SINGAPORE GIC SEES BETTER OPPORTUNITIES IN REAL ESTATE, PRIVATE EQUITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Government of Singapore Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or GIC, said Wednesday it sees more rewarding opportunities in real estate and private equity, and that it will continue investing in publicly listed equities as part of its emerging market strategy. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:AUSTRALIA'S REGIONAL DEVELOPMENT MINISTER SUPPORTS CHINESE INVESTMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Regional Development Minister Simon Crean Wednesday said he is a strong believer in foreign investment to help develop the country, given the historical lack of large domestic savings to fund investments and infrastructure development. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CARLOS SLIM SAYS AUSTRALIA, ASIA PACIFIC ARE VERY IMPORTANT RIGHT NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Carlos Slim, the world's richest man, said Wednesday that Australia and the Asia-Pacific region are very important but drew back from plans to make any investments in the region. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BAHT RISE STILL IN LINE WITH REGIONALS - THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Thailand Assistant Governor Suchada Kirakul said Wednesday the baht's strength is still in line with that of regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0604 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: THAI FINANCE MINISTRY EXPECTS GREATER FUND INFLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Wednesday it expects more funds to enter the country's financial markets, adding that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2 's recent comments suggesting the country's policy rate will rise have intensified inflows. (published 0654 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA SELLS MYR3.0 BLN SEP 2013 ISLAMIC BOND AT AVERAGE 3.199% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Malaysia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday sold MYR3.0 billion of September 2013 Government Islamic Issues at an average rate of 3.199%, slightly below the range of between 3.200% and 3.230% the market had expected. (published 0417 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA REVENUE SECRETARY: TO MEET TAX REVENUE AIM OF INR7.45 TLN THIS FY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's federal government expects to meet its tax revenue target of INR7.45 trillion for the current fiscal year that began April 1, Revenue Secretary Sunil Mitra said Wednesday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI FINANCE MINISTRY TO AUCTION THB90 BLN BONDS OCTOBER-DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai finance ministry plans to auction THB90 billion worth of government bonds in the first quarter of the next fiscal year, which starts Oct. 1, the head of the ministry's Public Debt Management Office, Chakkrit Parapuntakul, said Wednesday. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HYUNDAI AIMS TO SELL 5.5-YR BENCHMARK DOLLAR BOND TODAY-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Capital America\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to sell a benchmark-size 5.5-year dollar bond and aims to price the issue as soon as Wednesday, a person familiar with the deal said. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KEXIM LOOKING TO RAISE AROUND $1 BLN VIA GLOBAL BOND MID-NOVEMBER -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Export-Import Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or Kexim, is looking closely at global debt market conditions for a potential global bond sale in mid-November aimed at raising around $1 billion, a person familiar with its plan said Wednesday. (published 0013 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =ASIAN CENTRAL BANKS KEEP UP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS DOLLAR WEAKENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The central banks of South Korea, Singapore, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Indonesia were suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange markets Wednesday to contain gains in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but analysts say the continued weakness of the U.S. dollar means Asian units should extend their rallies. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =FOCUS: FOREIGNERS TO CONTINUE BUYING INDONESIAN GOV'T BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign investors have helped push Indonesian government bond yields to record lows, and likely will continue to snap up rupiah-denominated offerings in anticipation of a ratings upgrade. (published 0629 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: INDONESIA INFLATION LIKELY LOWER IN SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's inflation rate will likely be lower in September than the month before as the prices on most food items have started to decline following Muslim festivities that ended early this month. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: TAIWAN LIKELY TO RAISE POLICY RATE BY 12.5 BPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely raise its key policy interest rate by 12.5 basis points at its quarterly meeting Thursday as the local economy continues to recover despite a slowdown in global growth, with prices in the property market soaring. (published 0341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: TAIWAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LIKELY TO PAUSE AFTER THU \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is widely expected to hike policy interest rates by 12.5 basis points Thursday -- but after that it will most likely hold steady until at least the end of this year. (published 0453 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: MAPLETREE INDUSTRIAL TRUST PLANS S$1.2 BLN IPO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's Mapletree Industrial Trust said Wednesday it plans to raise as much as S$1.2 billion in gross proceeds from a sale of its units to retail, institutional and cornerstone investors, making it the country's second biggest initial public offering this year. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDUSTRIAL SECURITIES RAISES CNY2.63 BILLION VIA SHANGHAI IPO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese mid-sized brokerage \f28 \uc2 \f2 Industrial Securities Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . raised CNY2.63 billion after it priced its Shanghai initial public offering at CNY10.00 a share, the top end of the indicative range. (published 2350 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  HAS NO PLAN TO MOVE HEADQUARTERS TO HONG KONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's departing Chairman Stephen Green said Wednesday the banking giant has no plan to move its headquarters to Hong Kong from London, quelling recent market speculation about such a move. (published 0425 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WARREN BUFFETT: NO COMMENT ON IF PLANNING TO INCREASE STAKE IN BYD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Warren Buffett declined to comment Wednesday when asked by reporters if he was planning to increase his firm's stake in Chinese auto maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 BYD Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (1211.HK), saying only that "we love it." (published 0629 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NINTENDO: NEW 3DS GAME SYSTEM TO GO ON SALE IN JAPAN FEB 26 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nintendo Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it will launch its new 3DS handheld videogame system in February, damping speculation that it would launch the product in time for the year-end holiday shopping season. (published 0617 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PEUGEOT, MITSUBISHI SIGN NEW DEAL TO DEVELOP ELECTRIC CARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French auto maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 PSA Peugeot Citroen S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Motors Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday they have signed a new agreement to develop an electric version of the Peugeot Partner and Citroen Berlingo car models. (published 0614 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: DELL TO LAUNCH 7-INCH TABLET IN THE NEXT FEW WEEKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dell Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will launch its 7-inch tablet in the next few weeks and a 10-inch tablet within 6-12 months, Dell Greater China President Amit Midha said Wednesday. (published 0414 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DUET TO SELL DUQUESNE STAKE TO SINGAPORE'S GIC FOR US$360M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DUET Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday it has struck a deal to sell its 29% stake in Pennsylvania-based energy group Duquesne, or DQE Holdings LLC, to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Government of Singapore Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for US$360 million. (published 2345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S XINREN PLANS TO RAISE UP TO S$200 MLN IN SINGAPORE IPO - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China-based aluminum company Xinren is planning an initial public offering in Singapore which could be launched as early as October, people familiar with the situation said Wednesday. (published 0434 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SINGAPORE GIC SEES BETTER OPPORTUNITIES IN REAL ESTATE, PRIVATE EQUITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 29-09-10 0723GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Government of Singapore Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or GIC, said Wednesday it sees more rewarding opportunities in real estate and private equity, and that it will continue investing in publicly listed equities as part of its emerging market strategy. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: KB FINANCIAL PREPARES FOR OVERSEAS EXPANSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 KB Financial Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . must prepare to expand overseas to overcome slowing growth in the maturing domestic market, Chief Executive Euh Yoon-dae said Wednesday. (published 0119 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HYUNDAI WIA CORP PLANS S KOREA IPO, AIMS TO LIST IN MARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Hyundai Wia Corp., a unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Motor Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said Wednesday that it aims to go public in March. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: HYUNDAI TO CUT RELIANCE ON VESSEL-ENGINE SALES, RAISE PLANT ENGINE SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Heavy Industries\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the world's largest shipbuilder by orders, said Wednesday that it will cut its reliance on vessel-engine sales to less than 50% of total sales by 2015 due to shrinking demand from China, while ramping up sales of its plant engines division. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CITIC SECURITIES TO ESTABLISH FIRST WHOLLY-OWNED OFFSHORE SUBSIDIARY IN AUSTRALIA -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's largest investment bank, \f28 \uc2 \f2 CITIC Securities Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., is planning to set up its first wholly-owned offshore subsidiary in Australia to take advantage of burgeoning interest in the country's resources boom, a person familiar with the situation said Wednesday. (published 0329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 ASX LTD\f28 \uc2 \f2  CEO \f28 \uc2 \f2 ROBERT ELSTONE\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO STEP DOWN NEXT YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ASX Ltd., the operator of Australia's stock exchange, is on the hunt for a new chief executive after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Robert Elstone\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday he will step down around July next year. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: TELSTRA EYES FIRM BROADBAND DEAL BY YEAR END, OUTLINES STRATEGY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Telstra Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it hopes to finalize an agreement on the government's planned A$43 billion broadband network by the end of the year, as it outlined plans to spend A$1 billion to claw back market share in the mobile and broadband markets. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: QANTAS AIRWAYS CEO: INTERNATIONAL YIELD UP BY 12%-14% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alan Joyce\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday the carrier is seeing higher international yields but cautioned that business still remains challenging for the industry. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES RISE; TOKYO GETS LIFT FROM TANKAN SURVEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly higher Wednesday, with Japanese stocks boosted by a better-than-expected business sentiment survey. (published 0414 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA, RUSSIA IN TALKS OVER LOAN-FOR-GAS DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China may provide Russia with a large loan as part of a new long-term gas supply deal between the two countries, an executive from Russian state gas firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 OAO Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0621 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: ITOCHU TO ACT CAREFULLY IN CHINA AFTER DIPLOMATIC RIFT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese trading house \f28 \uc2 \f2 Itochu Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said it needs to be careful in its business dealings with China following a diplomatic standoff over the sovereignty of an East China Sea island chain, but added China has much to lose by disrupting bilateral trade. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SHAANXI TO REDUCE NUMBER OF COAL FIRMS; CONSOLIDATE SECTOR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Shaanxi province has pledged to reduce the number of coal exploration companies by the end of next June, down to 120 from 522, according to a statement on the official website of Shaanxi's provincial government. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SMX TO LAUNCH IRON ORE FUTURES CONTRACT; DATE NOT SPECIFIED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore Mercantile Exchange said Wednesday that it plans to launch a cash-settled iron-ore futures contract. (published 0121 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: VALE WILLING TO SET UP IRON-ORE DISTRIBUTION CENTER IN CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazilian miner Vale SA is willing to set up an iron ore distribution center in China if it is something the market needs, a senior company executive said Wednesday. (published 0443 GMT) [ 29-09-10 0723GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100929e69t000kg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
