\par\par \b \uc2 SE Asia Stocks-Indonesia at record high, Bangkok recovers\b0\par\par\uc2 675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 12:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments on baht policy soothe fears\par \par \uc2 * Inflows push Indonesia to record high\par \par \uc2 * Singapore recovers, around 2-year highs\par \par \uc2 By Viparat Jantraprap\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Sept 15 (Reuters) - Thai stocks ended flat on Wednesday, erasing losses after comments by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that helped soothe fears about the reimposition of capital controls, and Indonesia returned from a long holiday to hit a record high.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  Governor Tarisa Watanagase said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would curb volatility in the baht but saw no need to alter its present policy towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nSGE68E0AT]\par \par \uc2 Exporters and investors had worried that strength in the baht <THB=> would hurt Thai competitiveness, but the baht turned lower on Wednesday, in line with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after news that the Bank of Japan had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the yen's gains.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments eased earlier prevailing concerns about baht measures. Buying interest came across the board after that," said Pichai Lertsupongkij, head of sales at \uc2 Thanachart Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Thailand's benchmark stock index <.SETI> ended down 0.03 percent, but before the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2 's comment it had fallen as much as 2.05 percent to its lowest level since Aug. 31, extending a 1.7 percent fall on Tuesday as investors remembered tough capital controls that caused a stock market slump in 2006.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners sold a net $8.7 million of stocks on Wednesday, smaller than the net selling of $58.9 million of the previous session, according to the stock exchange.\par \par \uc2 Telecom stocks were among the gainers, with top mobile phone operator \uc2 Advanced Info Service\uc2  up 1.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 National carrier \uc2 Thai Airways\uc2  ended down 0.7 percent, earlier plunging 9 percent to a seven-week low after it offered new stock worth $488 million at a discount of 14.5 percent to the market, cheaper than analysts had expected. [ID:nSGE68E051]\par \par \uc2 Asian stocks in general were higher, with Tokyo <.N225> rising more than 2 percent after Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in six years to stem economic damage from the surging yen, pushing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sharply lower.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's broadest index of Asia-Pacific shares outside Japan <.MIAPJ0000PUS> eked out a small 0.45 percent gain by 0957 GMT.\par \par \uc2 Singapore <.FTSTI> rose 0.6 percent, reversing its loss of the previous day and hovering around two-year highs, while the Philippines <.PSI> edged up 0.13 percent to close to the record high set on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Malaysia <.KLSE> eased 0.1 percent ahead of a holiday on Thursday, still moving around 2-\u189\'00\'BD year high, and Vietnam <.VNI> inched down 0.06 percent.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's benchmark stock index <.JKSE> finished 3.9 percent higher, climbing to 3,359.99 at one point, topping the previous record set on Sept. 7 before the market shut for a long holiday.\par \par \uc2 Car seller \uc2 PT Astra International\uc2  , the biggest firm by market capitalisation, and state lender PT \uc2 Bank Mandiri\uc2  , both surged to a record high, rising 6.73 percent and 7.14 percent respectively.\par \par \uc2 Edwin Sebayang, head of research at PT Bhakti Securities in Jakarta, attributed the market rally to foreign buying and Indonesia's low interest rate environment.\par \par \uc2 "On the banking and auto move, market chatter says since this morning that most people in the market expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to hold rates next month, which created excitement as Astra, and the banks jumped," he said.\par \par \uc2 The Jakarta rally made the market Asia's second-best performer this year, ahead of number three the Philippines and Thailand, the fourth best.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia recorded inflows of $242.6 million on the session, the biggest daily net inflows in almost two years. Inflows rose to $1.86 billion in the year, compared with $936 million in full year 2009, Thomson Reuters data showed. (Additional reporting by Janeman Latul in Jakarta) (Editing by Alan Raybould)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SOUTHEASTASIA-STOCKS/|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|SI|IF|PHD|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100915e69f000oq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
