\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Singapore dlr hits record peak; won at 1-mth high\b0\par\par\uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2010\par 08:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Singapore dollar strength sparks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Thai baht at 13-year high, checked by c.bank\par \par \uc2 * Won hits 1-month high despite rates on hold\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Sept 9 (Reuters) - Increased fund inflows propelled the Singapore dollar to a record high on Thursday, while the South Korean won hit a one-month high despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surprise decision to keep interest rates steady.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar approached 15-year lows against the yen as traders bet that Japanese authorities are not yet ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the Australian dollar hit a four-month high on solid Australian jobs data. [ID:nTOE68805C]\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=D3> hits record high of 1.3411 per U.S. dollar, buoyed by fund inflows and a broadly weaker U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Traders suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars to contain the local unit's strength.\par \par \uc2 "The Singapore dollar looks to the rest of the region, and MAS is on the bid," a trader said.\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar, which is up 4.7 percent against the U.S. dollar this year, has been boosted by the country's solid economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners have been buying bonds and stocks, but the inflows are not as strong as elsewhere in the region, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> jumped 0.6 percent to a new 13-year high of around 30.83 per dollar, sparking fresh dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 Increasing capital inflows into Thai bonds and stocks in the past week have pushed the baht up 1 percent against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The baht dipped below 31.00 this morning and has so far risen to an intraday high of 30.83 before stabilising now at 30.87-89. Falling Thai bond yields today suggest that most of the funds are parked in local debt," a dealer at a foreign bank said.\par \par \uc2 The baht has appreciated 8.0 percent this year, the third-best Asian performer after yen and ringgit.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won hit a fresh one-month high despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surprise decision to leave interest rates on hold.\par \par \uc2 Investors reduced dollar-long positions, helping the won strengthen to as firm as 1,166.0, the strongest since Aug 10.\par \par \uc2 It pulled back slightly after the Bank of Korea unexpectedly held its benchmark rate steady for a second month as concerns mount about a slowing global recovery. [ID:nTOE68801V]\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> found support from exporters' demand for settlements and ended domestic trade at 1,167.4 per dollar compared to its previous close <KRW=KFTC> of 1,172.8. ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0632 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        83.67          83.85       +0.22\par  Sing dlr        1.3427         1.3443       +0.12\par  Taiwan dlr      31.894         31.979       +0.27\par  Korean won     1167.25        1172.80       +0.48\par  Baht             30.84          31.00       +0.52\par  Peso             44.10          44.2