\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Gilt/Bund Yield Spreads To Narrow Further\b0\par\par\uc2 1,335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2010\par 12:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1013 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts are outperforming bunds Friday following weak services PMI data, with the 10-year gilt/bund spread 2.6bps tighter at 65.80bps. The spread may still have more to tighten though, with Kenneth Broux at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lloyds TSB\f28 \uc2 \f2 , saying a move towards 60bps could happen in the near future. "Gilts should outperform bunds as a slowdown in the economy begins to materialize and in turn prompts the Bank of England to resume quantitative easing," Broux says. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1006 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PKR higher at 85.69 late Friday from 85.61 Thursday on higher demand from banks. USD received boost from banks covering positions ahead of weekend as banks they bet importer demand may take pair further up, says dealer. However, USD/PKR may ease from current levels as more IMF aid inflows expected over next week. For Monday though, pair likely in 85.65-85.75 band, dealer says. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1001 GMT [Dow Jones] Euro Overnight Index Average fixes lower Thursday at 0.364% vs Wednesday's 0.370%. Friday, one money dealer says trade is quiet and ample liquidity at the end of the minimum reserve period is putting rates under pressure. He adds that interbank overnight rates are a little lower between 0.26% and 0.30%. Earlier Friday, the 3-month Euribor fixed at 0.883%. (thomas.leppert@dowjones.com) Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 1000 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares end +1.0% at 929.90, closing higher for 7th straight session in highest volume in almost 11 months. Benchmark has gained 3.3% for week, lifting index to fresh almost 14-year-high, with volume above THB40 billion since last Friday. Court's Map Ta Phut ruling Thursday prompts industrial plays to take off but pace of rise likely to run out of gas next week, says \uc2 Kiatnakin Securities\uc2  analyst Apisit Limthumrongkul. Adds profit-taking expected to trim gains amid still positive sentiment in overall market; eyes on whether foreign investors will remain net buyers, in what amount. Tips 925-935 area. Among top actives, PTT (PTT.TH) +8.2% at THB291, PTT Aromatics & Refining (PTTAR.TH) +6.8% at THB25, \uc2 Siam Cement\uc2  (SCC.TH) +3.3% at THB313 though off intraday, historical high of THB321, Banpu (BANPU.TH) +1.3% at THB634. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0958 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai economic growth to slow to 3.5%-4.5% next year vs 7% forecast for 2010 due to weakening pace of global recovery, says \uc2 Siam Commercial Bank\uc2 's Economic Intelligence Center; Chief Economist Sethaput Suthiwart-Narueput says recent global strength propelled by one-off factors including stimulus measures, inventory rebuilding, but adds they're now wearing off, which will trim export expansion. "Unfortunately, domestic demand is unlikely to be able to fill the gap as the overall environment next year is not that conducive to rapid growth in private demand: the THB will be stronger, interest rates and oil prices will be higher, and the overhang of political uncertainty is likely to remain." (leigh.murray@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0954 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds remain higher but steady after cut-offs at INR120 billion auction largely in-line with expectations, says trader with state-run bank. Benchmark 7.80% 2020 bond at 98.96 vs 98.99 before auction cut-offs, 98.80 last close. "The market has been quite stable. The market is now comforted because fears over bonds turning illiquid have been taken care of by issuing the 8.08% 2022 bond," trader says. Notes, some traders may book profits but buying interest to emerge in benchmark 2020 bond from here. Tips benchmark 2020 bond in 98.80-99.15 band in session. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0947 GMT [Dow Jones] The safe haven favorites, CHF, JPY and the dollar are slipping in light trade ahead of the U.S. August nonfarm payrolls at 1230 GMT even though most analysts are looking for a downbeat outcome. European equity markets are holding gains of around 0.5% which might explain some of the improvement in risk appetite in Europe. EUR/CHF rises to a September high of 1.3042, USD/JPY is at the day's high of 84.44 as is EUR/JPY at 108.42, EUR/USD at 1.2846 and USD/CHF at 1.0159. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0941 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/CZK trades slightly higher at 24.693-24.718 from 24.69 late Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair stagnates amid a mixed equity market, a trader says. EUR/CZK is set to remain around 24.70 midday Friday as investors wait for U.S. jobless data at 1230 GMT, which will likely influence EUR/USD and, in turn, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to follow the euro's moves, the trader adds. (sean.carney@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0926 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR touch lower at 9,003 late vs 9,008 yesterday as foreign funds enter stock market after Bank Indonesia kept policy rate unchanged at 6.50%, dealers say. "Many foreign names were buying IDR in the last minutes of trade, I guess to buy shares," dealer at local bank says; tips pair in 8,980-9,010 range Monday. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0926 GMT 0925 GMT [Dow Jone[Dow Jones Chief Technical Analyst For Europe. (francis.bray@dowjones.com) (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security or \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 0925 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/THB nudges higher to 31.16 vs 31.15 late yesterday in Asia on suspected heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  after pair slipped to 31.13 early, dealers say, though trade otherwise thinning out as market becomes cautious after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it may use certain measures, if necessary, to stem THB's rapid rise. Market also eyeing U.S. non-farm payrolls due later today. "The BOT was buying in quite large amounts, but I don't think the rebound will last and I think we could see the THB even try and test 31.00 next week," says Bangkok-based trader. Support next week tipped at 31.00, resistance at 31.30. (leigh.murray@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0925 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD is looking to put pressure on Wednesday's high at 1.2856, and a break higher towards the 1.2900 level is the main threat. The August 18 lower high at 1.2923 lies above there, and upside scope exists to the 1.618 extension target at 1.2936. Failure to break above 1.2856 would prompt downside consolidation towards Thursday's low at 1.2776, but only a sustained break below there would concern bulls. EUR/USD is at 1.2844. - By Francis Bray, Dow Jones Chief Technical Analyst For Europe.(francis.bray@dowjones.com) (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security or \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 09-03-10 0613ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100903e69300071\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
