\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Fin Min:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  May Raise Rates 25 Bps This Year -CNBC\b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2010\par 02:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may hike its policy interest rate by 25 basis points before the year ends to cool the domestic economy, Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said Monday.\par \par \uc2 "If there are signs that the global economy is going to turn negative in a significant manner, that may be reason for the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  maybe to have another increase and then wait and see from there on," Korn told CNBC television.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's future actions would depend on economic data over the next month or so, he said. The benchmark rate has been raised twice by 25 basis points to 1.75% this year, he said.\par \par \uc2 The finance minister said the baht remains competitive even after rising by as much as 5.5% against the U.S. dollar as other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have also strengthened.\par \par \uc2 The weakness in the U.S. dollar has prompted the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise recently.\par \par \uc2 The baht hit a two-year high against the U.S. dollar Friday.\par \par \uc2 -By Gaurav Raghuvanshi and Costas Paris; Dow Jones Newswires; +65 64154 154; gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com [ 30-08-10 0115GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100830e68u0002c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
