\par\par \b \uc2 FXNEWS-Baht eases, tracking weaker Asian stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 170 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2010\par 05:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Thai baht <THB=> has opened a shade stronger than late Monday but a broad dollar rally against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed it down to around 31.50-52 per dollar. "The baht started at 31.48-49, but \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise it has pushed it back to 31.49-51. The BOT action should help keep it above 31.40 for a while," a Bangkok-based trader said. A second dealer said broad consolidation of Asian stocks this week reflected market caution amid uncertain U.S. and euro zone economic pictures. Dollar/baht was bid at 31.48 at 0246 GMT against 31.47 late on Monday. Despite its morning consolidation, the baht has appreciated 1.9 percent against the dollar in the past month and 5.8 percent this year, the third best Asian performer after the yen and ringgit.\par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: vithoon.amorn.reuters.com@reuters.net\par \par \uc2 LANGEN|ABN|M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100824e68o0003m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
