\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  seen as won, peso hit 11-week highs\b0\par\par\uc2 878 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2010\par 08:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Won, peso lead most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher against dollar\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen in Korea, \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Philippines\par \par \uc2  * Dlr/yuan NDFs off 2-week low amid policy uncertainty\par \par \uc2  By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 3 (Reuters) - The South Korean won and Philippine peso hit 11-week highs on Tuesday as upbeat U.S. factory data and European bank earnings buoyed risk-taking, but their gains were curtained by official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Asian stocks rose to their highest in nearly three months and turned positive for the year, while the dollar hovered near a three-month low against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  <.DXY>.\par \par \uc2  Earnings from big European banks \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2   and \uc2 HSBC\uc2   topped forecasts as bad debt fell sharply.\par \par \uc2 U.S. manufacturing grew in July for a 12th straight month, an industry report showed on Monday. Although growth slowed, it was still stronger than had been expected. [ID:nN02170396]\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  The won <KRW=> gained as much as percent 1,159.9 per dollar, the highest since May 19, but later pared most gains as the authorities were spotted buying dollars, causing some investors to cover dollar-short positions.\par \par \uc2  Still, traders expect the won <KRW=> to rise further.    "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the beginning prompt some offshore players to buy dollars, preventing the won's further gains. But it is unlikely to get back to the 1,170 levels after breaking through major resistance lines," said a foreign bank dealer.\par \par \uc2  Another foreign bank dealer said: "It is difficult to buy the won further as the authorities may -- be able to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more easily once exporters deals are completed."\par \par \uc2  Foreign investors bought a net 132.7 billion won worth of stocks on the main exchange, helping the benchmark KOSIP <.KS11> rise nearly 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2  PESO\par \par \uc2  Dollar/peso NDFs fell across the curve as hedge funds and other offshore investors were seen dumping dollars, particularly in short tenors.\par \par \uc2  "Offshore investors expect lower spot rates," said a NDF trader.\par \par \uc2  The most liquid one-month dollar/peso NDFs <PHP1MNDFOR=> hit a 2-\u189\'00\'BD   month low at 45.32 from 45.39 late on Monday, while one-month onshore forwards <PHP1M=> fell to 45.365 from 45.496.\par \par \uc2  The onshore/offshore spread narrowed to 45 points from 106 points on Monday.\par \par \uc2  Spot peso <PHP=> gained 0.4 percent to 45.13 to the dollar, the highest in 11 weeks, but it later pulled back to 45.20 as traders spotted dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  YUAN\par \par \uc2  Dollar/yuan NDFs <CNYNDFOR=> dropped to a two-week low but later rebounded slightly as uncertainty over China's yuan policy kept markets trading within an established range.\par \par \uc2  "People are more willing to take risk but there are still no signs China will speed up appreciation in the yuan," said a trader at an Asian bank in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2  He said activity remains thin and driven by trade-related hedging rather than speculation.\par \par \uc2  One-year NDFs bounced to 6.6744 from two-week low of 6.6560 in early trade and from late-Monday's 6.6645 to price in 12-month yuan appreciation of 1.47 percent.\par \par \uc2  The one-year NDF has fluctuated in a range of yuan appreciation between 1.3 percent and 1.9 percent since late-June.\par \par \uc2  BAHT\par \par \uc2  The Thai baht <THB=> gained slightly to 32.15 per dollar, with some traders seeing signs of \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  bids for dollars at 32.18.\par \par \uc2  "The BOT is on the bid side at around 32.18/19 but the volume is still thin. If the current trend drags on, the baht could gradually appreciate until the BOT's next policy rate review on Aug. 25 when it may raise rates again," said a dealer in Bangkok.\par \par \uc2  "But this does not mean there won't be some consolidation along the way," added the dealer.  Change on the day at 0607 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        86.41          86.46       +0.06\par  Sing dlr        1.3521         1.3486       -0.26\par  Taiwan dlr      31.785         31.868       +0.26\par  Korean won     1171.40        1172.50       +0.09\par  Baht             32.19          32.20       +0.03\par  Peso             45.21          45.33       +0.27\par  Rupiah         8943.00        8940.00       -0.03\par  Rupee            46.22          46.24       +0.05\par  Ringgit         3.1625         3.1595       -0.09\par  Yuan            6.7736         6.7742       +0.01\par  Change so far in 2010\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        86.41          92.90       +7.51\par  Sing dlr        1.3521         1.4053       +3.93\par  Taiwan dlr      31.785         32.030       +0.77\par  Korean won     1171.40        1164.50       -0.59\par  Baht             32.19          33.32       +3.51\par  Peso             45.21          46.20       +2.19\par  Rupiah         8943.00        9420.00       +5.33\par  Rupee            46.22          46.54       +0.69\par  Ringgit         3.1625      