\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won rallies on inflows, baht at 6-wk high\b0\par\par\uc2 804 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 08:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Refiles to fix typo in first graph)\par \par \uc2 * Won nears one-week high on foreign stock buying\par \par \uc2 * Baht jumps after holiday, official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected\par \par \uc2 * Rupiah bucks firmer Asia as local corporates buy dollars\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, March 2 (Reuters) - The South Korean won rose on Tuesday as investors turned back to riskier assets, while the Thai baht jumped in tandem with local stocks as investors reacted positively to a court ruling on former Prime Minister Thaksin.\par \par \uc2 Asian shares rose for a third straight session, lending some support to regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although investors' sentiment remain fragile amid doubts over a quick solution to Greece's debt problems, which weighed on the euro. [IDnSGE62103Y].\par \par \uc2 Sterling fell, staying under pressure after hitting a 10-month low the previous day, while the Australian dollar slipped, giving back earlier gains made after an interest rate rise by Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nTOE62105A]\par \par \uc2 The Aussie had initially climbed after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  raised interest rates by 25 basis points to 4.0 percent and flagged further hikes ahead.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The won <KRW=> gained 1 percent to 1,148.6 per dollar --\par the highest in nearly a week -- as foreign investors snapped up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 local stocks, but dollar/won NDFs were rangebound as offshore players remained cautious.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean markets were shut on Monday for holiday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It seems the market is taking on some risk today, so dollar/won is sold down," said a Singapore-based trader.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Seoul shares <.KS11> rose just over 1 percent as foreigners bought a net 72.5 billion won worth of stocks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data showing Korean exports per working day soared to a 17-month peak in February also supported sentiment, traders said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One-month NDFs <KRW1MNDFOR=> was confined between 1,152 and 1,162 in slow trade.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BAHT\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The baht <THB=> jumped 1 percent from Friday to its highest in six weeks as investors returned from a holiday on Monday and took comfort from a court ruling on the assets of ousted Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra on Friday [ID:nSGE61P02B].\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The baht rose as far as 32.72 per dollar, despite suspected official \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to temper its strength.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We believe the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  entered the market at around 32.80 but its limited efforts could not halt the rally. The baht is benefiting from more capital inflows to Thai stocks," a Bangkok-based dealer said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai stock index <SETI> rose 0.94 percent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A second trader also believed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , attributing baht gains to market relief that the court ruling on Friday had not triggered any violent reaction from his supporters [ID:nSGE61P02B].\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RUPIAH\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the rupiah <IDR=> bucked the firm trend in Asia.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The high-yielding unit fell half of a percent to 9,295 per dollar as some local corporates bought dollars to pay for their imports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most corporates had fulfiled their month-end settlements, but some had held off dollar buying in anticipation for lower dollar/rupiah, traders said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rupiah rose to 9,250 on Monday as investors bought the unit ahead of a government bond auction on Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The dollar/rupiah level was good enough, so they started buying," said a Jakarta-based trader.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some investors bought dollars ahead of the daily NDF fixing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, one-month dollar/rupiah NDFs <IDR1MNDFOR=> inched up to 9,330 from 9,270 late on Monday. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0700 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        89.31          89.09       -0.25\par  Sing dlr        1.4056         1.4057       +0.01\par  Taiwan dlr      32.017         32.048       +0.10\par  Korean won     1151.55        1160.00       +0.73\par  Baht             32.78          33.06       +0.85\par  Peso             46.09          46.12       +0.07\par  Rupiah         9300.00        9250.00       -0.54\par  Rupee            46.03          46.09       +0.13\par  Ringgit         3.3850         3.3875       +0.07\par  Yuan            6.8276         6.8263       -0.02\par  Change so far in 2010\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        89.31          92.90       +4.02\par  Sing dlr        1.4056         1.4053       -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr      32.017         32.030       +0.04\par  Korean won     1151.55        1164.50       +1.12\par  Baht             32.78          33.32       +1.65\par  Peso             46.09          46.20       +0.25\par  Rupiah         9300.00        9420.00       +1.29\par  Rupee            46.03          46.54       +1.11\par 