\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Fin Min: Government Backs  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's Plan To Ease  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Rules\b0\par\par\uc2 167 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2010\par 08:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said Friday that the government supports a plan by the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  to ease \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules to help boost capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 "The factor that the BOT and the government are keeping an eye on is that we don't want the baht to lose competitiveness with trading counterparts," he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  Governor Tarisa Watanagase announced plans to ease the rules Thursday during her annual policy speech.\par \par \uc2 The move comes at a time when the baht is under appreciation pressure, in tandem with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which could lessen the need for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's regular \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Bandid Nijathaworn told reporters Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will unveil the details of the rule changes on Monday at 0700 GMT.\par \par \uc2 -By Leigh Murray, Dow Jones Newswires; 66-2690-4200; leigh.murray@dowjones.com [ 29-01-10 0807GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100129e61t0017n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
