\par\par \b \uc2 Thai stocks may open higher, but wary over politics\b0\par\par\uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2010\par 03:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Jan 5 (Reuters) - Thai stocks are expected to track foreign bourses higher on Tuesday after optimism over the U.S. economy pushed Wall Street to a 15-month high, and energy stocks should rise after a jump in oil prices, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 But any gains may be capped by worries about the domestic political situation, which is likely to become more tense with anti-government rallies planned this month, they added.\par \par \uc2 "The index should bounce back, the main drivers coming from positive moves in overseas markets and a leap in world oil prices. Energy shares should rebound and push up the index," said Therdsak Taveeteeratham, a senior analyst with Asia Plus Securities.\par \par \uc2 Resistance on the main index <.SETI> is expected at 740 and support at 725, he said.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the benchmark SET index started the new year with a small drop, down 0.31 percent to 732.28, weighed down by profit-taking in energy and banking shares.\par \par \uc2 Click [TH/TRADING01] for cumulative trading value by \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investor type. ----------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT @ 0005 GMT\par ------------\par                  INSTRUMENT   LAST       PCT CHG   NET CHG\par S&P 500             <.SPX>       1132.99       1.6%    17.890\par USD/JPY             <JPY=>       92.41        -0.1%    -0.090\par 10-YR US TSY YLD    <US10YT=RR>  3.8232          --    -0.014\par SPOT GOLD           <XAU=>       1119.9      -0.10%    -1.100\par US CRUDE            <CLc1>       81.67        0.20%     0.160\par DOW JONES           <.DJI>       10583.96     1.50%    155.91\par ASIA ADRS           <.BKAS>      130.97       2.57%      3.28\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par MARK