\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso, won lead Asian rally; central banks in\b0\par\par\uc2 952 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2009\par 07:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Peso leads Asia rally, rises to 2-week high\par \par \uc2 * Korean won up, renewed foreign interest in won assets\par \par \uc2 * Baht extends gains in thin trade ahead of king's birthday\par \par \uc2 By Vithoon Amorn\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso and South Korean won led the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally on Wednesday as investors gradually resumed buying of risky assets, with concerns easing over Dubai's debt problems that dimmed dollar's safe-haven allure and boosted the yen and gold.\par \par \uc2 But the yen <JPY=> fell 0.28 percent against a defensive dollar to 86.97, far below its 14-year high of 84.82 last week, as investors weighed steps taken by Bank of Japan on Tuesday to attack deflationary pressures that left many disappointed [ID:nT181057].\par \par \uc2 The dollar index <.DXY> fell to 74.41 from 74.46 late on Tuesday but well above its recent 15-mth low of 74.14.\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> rallied 0.75 percent to a two-week high of 46.50 per dollar from a Tuesday close of 46.86, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the day to curb gains.\par \par \uc2 "BSP is in the market, seen buying dollars at around 46.80-60. Volume is normal in mostly one-way trade dominated by dollar sellers," a trader in Manila said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the broad dollar weakness and inflows of remittances sent by Filipino workers abroad lifted the peso. They believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pursuing a policy of trying to keep peso in a broad 46.00-49.00 range.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been suspected of reacting to recent peso rallies by trying to restrain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 46.45 and 46.25. Peso has gained about 2.17 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=> extended gains, tracking stocks and a revival in appetite for won assets. Although investors grew more cautious over possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.\par \par \uc2 Some suspected the authorities of absorbing dollars to cap the gains. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 1,153.8 per dollar, compared with its domestic close <KRW=KFTC> of 1,161.1 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "Foreigners are buying local stocks, supporting the won, but its gains would be limited by the authorities' smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a bank dealer.\par \par \uc2 The Korean Composite Stock Price Index <.KS11> closed up 1.4 percent at its highest level in a week and nearly recovered losses suffered on fears sparked by the Dubai debt woes. [ID:nSEO175445]\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> was among Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firming against the dollar, rising to a one-week high of 33.15 from 33.18 late on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "The market should be very thin today as we are in a holiday mood, which will keep the baht in a narrow range tracking bullish Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a trader in Bangkok said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers did not detect any \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but said the thin volume would have made it easy for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push baht back to 33.20 if it wanted to.\par \par \uc2 Thailand is celebrating King Bhumibol Adulyadej's 82nd birthday over the next two weeks. Monday is a public holiday. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0532 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        86.97          86.73       -0.28\par  Sing dlr        1.3794         1.3810       +0.12\par  Taiwan dlr      32.129         32.199       +0.22\par  Korean won     1153.80        1161.10       +0.63\par  Baht             33.15          33.18       +0.09\par  Peso             46.51          46.86       +0.75\par  Rupiah         9425.00        9440.00       +0.16\par  Rupee            46.20          46.31       +0.24\par  Ringgit         3.3745         3.3785       +0.12\par  Yuan            6.8265         6.8260       -0.01\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        86.97          90.60       +4.17\par  Sing dlr        1.3794         1.4340       +3.96\par  Taiwan dlr      32.129         32.860       +2.28\par  Korean won     1153.80        1259.50       +9.16\par  Baht             33.15          34.80       +4.98\par  Peso             46.51          47.52       +2.17\par  Rupiah         9425.00       11000.00      +16.71\par  Rupee            46.20          48.71       +5.43\par  Ringgit         3.3745         3.4500       +2.24\par  Yuan            6.8265         6.8230       -0.05\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Cheon Jongwoo in Seoul; Editing by Jan Dahinten) ((vithoon.amorn.reuters.com; Reuters Messaging: vithoon.amorn.reuters.com@reuters.net; 662-6489737)) ((If you have a query or comment on this story, send an email to news.feedback.asia@thomsonreuters.com)) For the new Reuters scrolling global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  service plea