\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,035 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2009\par 08:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: ASIAN CENTRAL BANKS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO LIMIT DOLLAR'S SLIDE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Singapore and South Korea appeared to sell their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday, fending off the dollar's slide that threatens their export-oriented economies. But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were small, reflecting a view that Asian authorities are powerless in halting a broad sell-off in the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0545 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN FUJII SHOWS CONCERN AS YEN AT 14-YEAR HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister said Thursday that he is watching the yen's upward trend "very carefully," suggesting he is becoming more concerned about the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise after it hit a 14-year high against the dollar. (published 0537 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN 3Q CAPEX FALLS, BUT OUTLOOK STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business investment fell sharply in the third quarter but the outlook for capital spending remained strong as companies expect an upswing in the economy in 2010. (published 0441 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: SINGAPORE OCTOBER MANUFACTURING GREW WEAKER THAN EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's manufacturing output expanded in October, mainly due to strength in the electronics sector, but the pace of growth fell below expectations as pharmaceutical production remained sluggish. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : GOVT TO ASK STATE COS TO SELL DOLLARS TO BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Vietnamese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday the government will ask state-owned companies to sell their dollar holdings to banks to help boost foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  liquidity. (published 0224 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI MINISTER: DONG DEVALUATION WON'T AFFECT THAI ECON MUCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's decision to devalue its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will have little impact on the Thai economy, Thai Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said Thursday. (published 0423 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: BANK INDONESIA RAISES 2009 GROWTH FORECAST AS OUTLOOK IMPROVES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia Thursday raised its economic growth forecast for this year as improving investment, domestic demand and exports brighten the country's outlook. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: BOJ OPEN TO REUSING SPECIAL LENDING FACILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan may reuse a special lending facility due to expire at the end of March if corporate fundraising conditions deteriorate, minutes of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Oct. 30 policy board meeting showed Thursday. (published 0148 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: PHILIPPINE GDP RISES 0.8% ON YEAR IN THIRD QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine economic growth slowed in the third quarter, losing some steam on a decline in manufacturing and a sluggish farm sector. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : READY TO PROVIDE FURTHER POLICY STIMULUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday that it is ready to provide further policy stimulus if needed, especially with inflation still tracking targets set by the monetary authorities. (published 0347 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA BOND WITHHOLDING TAX PLAN PASSES SENATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian lawmakers on Thursday passed legislation that, once it receives royal assent, will remove interest withholding tax on federal debt securities. (published 0415 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA TSYS LIKELY TO BE INCLUDED IN GLOBAL INDEX EARLY 2010-SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The much-talked-about inclusion of South Korean treasuries in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2 's World Government Bond Index is most likely to take place early next year, people familiar with the matter said. (published 0330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PERUSAHAAN LISTRIK: PLAN DOLLAR, RUPIAH BOND DEALS NEXT YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesian state electricity provider \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Perusahaan Listrik Negara\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to issue dollar- and rupiah-denominated bonds next year to raise funds for a capacity expansion program, the company's president director said Thursday. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: S KOREA TO WIDEN INFLATION-TARGET BAND; NO RATE HIKE SEEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  widened its annual inflation target band, giving it greater flexibility in using monetary policy to cope with economic uncertainties. (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ BUSINESS CONFIDENCE SLIPS IN NOVEMBER BUT STILL ROBUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business confidence in New Zealand slipped for the second successive month but remained relatively robust in November, according to a survey, reinforcing recent evidence that the economic recovery remains on track. (published 0302 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:NZ BUDGET UPDATE TO CONFIRM RECESSION IMPACT -MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand Finance Minister Bill English said Thursday the government will publish its half-yearly economic and fiscal update on Dec. 15, which will confirm the impact of a recently ended recession on the government's finances. (published 2327 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA AIMS TO DOUBLE FOREIGN DIRECT INVESTMENT IN 5 YEARS-REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's Investment Coordinating Board hopes to increase foreign direct investment in the country to $25 billion-$35 billion a year from an expected $15 billion this year, the Jakarta Globe reported Thursday, citing the board's chairman. (published 0550 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM NOVEMBER TRADE DEFICIT $1.75 BLN VS $1.9 BLN IN OCTOBER - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's trade deficit narrowed 7.9% from a month earlier to $1.75 billion in November, state media said Thursday. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM JAN-NOV FOREIGN DIRECT INVESTMENT DISBURSEMENTS $9 BLN -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign direct investment disbursements in Vietnam in the first 11 months of this year reached $9 billion, representing 89.6% of the target set for the year, state media said Thursday. (published 0316 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA DEC MANUFACTURERS OUTLOOK INDEX FALLS TO 4-MONTH LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean manufacturers' business outlook worsened for a second straight month to a four-month low in December as exporters were worried that the appreciating won may hurt their profitability and damp demand, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  survey released Thursday showed. (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: TAIWAN OKS NT$3.99 TLN FOR INFRASTRUCTURE OVER 8 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Taiwan cabinet approved Thursday an eight-year, NT$3.99 trillion infrastructure development plan involving 12 projects proposed by President Ma Ying-jeou during his election campaign in 2008. (published 0444 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: DLR/YEN OPTIONS UP AS DLR FALLS, BUT LEVELS LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen options rose in Tokyo on Thursday due to increased demand for hedges as the underlying exchange rate fell close to a 14-year low. (published 0324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =GLOBAL YIELD:HONG KONG SNAPS UP TREASURYS TO DEFEND DOLLAR PEG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong, the world's seventh-largest holder of foreign reserves, has become one of the biggest buyers of Treasury securities outside the U.S. this year as local officials stepped up efforts to defend the 26-year-old \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg. (published 1855 GMT) [ 26-11-09 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091126e5bq000ge\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
