\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Baht Rises To Fresh 17-Month High Against Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 151 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2009\par 02:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht rose to a fresh 17-month high against the dollar in moderate trade Thursday, and the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's climb, local dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was quoted at THB33.17-THB33.18 late Wednesday but the rapid fall of the greenback against the euro led the dollar to slip against the baht in overnight trade. As of 0134 GMT, the dollar was trading at THB33.11.\par \par \uc2 "Players are well aware of the bearish tone of the dollar....The dollar/baht may slip through 33.00 near term," said one dealer, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have stepped in to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but is unlikely to try reverse the tide.\par \par \uc2 -By Piyarat Setthasiriphaiboon, Dow Jones Newswires; 66 2 2660744; piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com [ 26-11-09 0136GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091126e5bq0003f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
