\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso firms on trade data, Vietnam devalues dong\b0\par\par\uc2 937 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2009\par 08:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Peso spot rises 0.7 pct, NDF/onshore spreads widen\par \par \uc2 * Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ride on broad dollar weakness\par \par \uc2 * Vietnam devalues dong, 1-year NDFs imply 13 pct dong fall\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Nov 25 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso led Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher on Wednesday against a broadly weaker dollar, while Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the market by announcing its third \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation since mid-2008.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to its lowest in seven weeks against the Japanese yen, while the Australian dollar rose after a central banker made upbeat comments on the economy. [ID:nT352975]\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 The peso <PHP=> gained almost 0.7 percent to 46.75 to the dolla as investors took comfort from data which showed a narrowing trade deficit in September. [ID:nMAN516448]\par \par \uc2 "The peso is getting a boost on that early news," said a Manila-based dealer, adding that offshore players could be more aggressive in selling dollars given that non-deliverable forwards have been at a discount versus onshore forwards.\par \par \uc2 Dollar/peso NDFs <PHPNDFOR=> moved lower across the curve while some traders see heavier selling at 1-year tenor.\par \par \uc2 Three-month dollar/peso NDFs eased to 47.04, implying a 0.6 percent peso fall. Meanwhile, onshore forwards with the same tenor <PHP3M=> eased to 47.183, pricing in a 0.9 percent peso fall.\par \par \uc2 Spreads between the NDFs and forwards widened to -0.143 from -0.083 at Tuesday's close.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The baht <THB=> rose a fifth of a percent to 33.15 per dollar but suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrained its gains.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still in the market to try to smooth out the baht's volatility to around 33.20," said a Bangkok-based dealer of a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 Traders said a possible move by supporters of ousted Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra to postpone their planned anti-government rally this weekend [ID:nBKK486658] could lift market sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Baht has gained 0.8 percent so far this month and 4.9 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Tarisa Watanagase said the bank had no timeframe for any interest rate rise because there was still risks to the economy. [ID:nBKK526348]\par \par \uc2 DONG\par \par \uc2 Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided on Wednesday to devalue the dong <VDN=> by 5.44 percent, narrow its trading band and raise interest rates in a dramatic bid to stem persistent pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken. [ID:nSP394910]\par \par \uc2 Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday's mid-point reference rate for dong transactions on the interbank market would be 17,961 per dollar, which compared to Wednesday's rate at 17,034.\par \par \uc2 Non-deliver forwards in illiquid offshore market still point to further dong weakness despite the devaluation.\par \par \uc2 One-year dollar/dong NDFs <PNDG> hovered near 20,600, implying a further 13 percent fall from the new mid-point rate.\par \par \uc2 Since January, the dong had fallen almost 13 percent on unofficial markets from about 17,500 dong per dollar to 19,700/19,900 per dollar on Wednesday before the announcement. After the news, it strengthened to 19,500/19,700 in Hanoi. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0702 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        88.29          88.56       +0.31\par  Sing dlr        1.3822         1.3855       +0.24\par  Taiwan dlr      32.234         32.288       +0.17\par  Korean won     1152.25        1156.80       +0.39\par  Baht             33.19          33.23       +0.12\par  Peso             46.77          47.06       +0.62\par  Rupiah         9420.00        9475.00       +0.58\par  Rupee            46.30          46.37       +0.15\par  Ringgit         3.3740         3.3770       +0.09\par  Yuan            6.8283         6.8294       +0.02\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        88.29          90.60       +2.62\par  Sing dlr        1.3822         1.4340       +3.75\par  Taiwan dlr      32.234         32.860       +1.94\par  Korean won     1152.25        1259.50       +9.31\par  Baht             33.19          34.80       +4.85\par  Peso             46.77          47.52       +1.60\par  Rupiah         9420.00       11000.00      +16.77\par  Rupee            46.30          48.71       +5.21\par  Ringgit         3.3740         3.4500       +2.25\par  Yuan            6.8283         6.8230       -0.08\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Kevin Yao) ((kevin.yao@thomsonreuters.com; +65 6870 3841; Reuters Messaging: kevin.yao.reuters.com@reuters.net )) ((If you have a query or comment on this story, send an email to news.feedback.asia@thomsonreuters.com)) For the new Reuters scrolling global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  service please click <FXNEWS> ((Multimedia versions of Reuters Top News are now available for: * 3000 Xtra : visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK