\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,065 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2009\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BOJ UPGRADES ECONOMIC VIEW FOR 3RD STRAIGHT MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan policy board, in a surprise move, Friday revised up its assessment of the broad economy for the third straight month. (published 0458 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: KAN SAYS JAPAN IN DEFLATION, TO TELL VIEW TO BOJ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's deputy prime minister acknowledged Friday that the nation's economy is in a deflationary phase and that the government will convey its view to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0236 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: PBOC: CHINA SPURRING DEMAND; EYE ON INVESTMENT, HOUSING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China Gov. Zhou Xiaochuan said Friday that China is making progress on stimulating domestic demand, but also signaled the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is paying attention to the surge in investment and housing demand. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: EX-PBOC WU: REQUIRED RESERVE RATIO MAY CHANGE - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A former China central banker said the People's Bank of China could adjust banks' reserve requirement ratio next year, but played down expectations of monetary policy reversing course as the recovery in the domestic economy continues to take hold, a state-run newspaper reported Friday. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:THAI EXPORTS FELL MARGINALLY IN OCTOBER; TO GROW IN 4Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's crucial export sector continues to show signs of recovery, with customs-basis exports in October shrinking at their slowest pace so far this year, the Ministry of Commerce said Friday. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US LAWMAKERS THREATEN SANCTIONS ON CHINA OVER \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. lawmakers criticized U.S. President Barack Obama's administration Thursday for not pressuring China enough over its rigid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as they set the stage for slapping import duties on Chinese goods. (published 0153 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FED PLOSSER: NOT QUITE TIME YET TO RAISE INTEREST RATES -CNBC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It's not "quite time yet" to raise interest rates, Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia President Charles Plosser said in an interview aired Friday on CNBC. (published 0014 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CONSISTENTLY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET-MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said Friday that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has consistently \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in the past several months to ensure that the baht's pace of appreciation is gradual. (published 0550 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HKMA: 2010 ASSET PRICES MAY RISE SHARPLY; RISK OF ASSET BUBBLES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's asset prices could rise sharply next year and increase the risk of bubbles forming in the economy, Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Chief Executive Norman Chan said Thursday. (published 0328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF KOREA: NEED TO CLOSELY MONITOR PROPERTY MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea said Friday that there is a need to continue closely monitoring the property market for any signs of asset price bubbles. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S PRUDENTIAL SUPERVISOR CAUTIONS IN OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The operating environment for Australia's banks will remain testing for some time to come and market sentiment could easily turn sour again, Australia's prudential regulator warned Friday. (published 0321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES 3RD-QUARTER GROWTH LIKELY 1.6%-2.6% ON YEAR-REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines' gross domestic product likely picked up pace in the third quarter, expanding between 1.6%-2.6% from a year earlier on stronger consumer spending because of steady growth in overseas workers remittance, BusinessWorld reported Friday, quoting acting Economic Planning Secretary Augusto Santos. (published 0217 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN KAMEI: DEBT MORATORIUM WOULD HAVE TIMELY IMPACT - NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Shizuka Kamei said that he will do his utmost to see the debt moratorium bill quickly pass the Diet, arguing that it would have a positive impact on firms as the year-end approaches, the Nikkei reported Friday. (published 0131 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA FSS GOVERNOR:GOVT MAY REVIEW MEANS TO DEAL WITH CARRY TRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government may review means to deal with dollar-carry trade, which is viewed as a cause of volatility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the Financial Supervisory Service Governor Kim Jong-chang said late Thursday. (published 2300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FRANCE'S \f28 \uc2 \f2 GDF SUEZ\f28 \uc2 \f2  PLANS TO OFFER Y30B 5-YEAR SAMURAI BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French energy company \f28 \uc2 \f2 GDF Suez\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to offer Y30 billion worth of five-year Samurai bonds next month, documents filed at Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed Friday. (published 0221 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BUMI SOLD $300 MLN OF 7-YEAR CONVERTIBLE BOND;5.75% YIELD-BANKERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Bumi Resources\f28 \uc2 \f2  has sold $300 million of seven-year convertible bond on Thursday at a yield of 5.75%, according to bankers Friday. (published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROYAL BANK OF SCOTLAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRICES 15-MONTH A$2.0B GUARANTEED BOND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Royal Bank of Scotland Group Plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Australia branch on Friday raised A$2.0 billion through an issue of 15-month government-guaranteed bonds. (published 0132 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: FED'S FISHER SEES 3Q GDP REVISED DOWN TO 2.5%-3% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. economy expanded by less than estimated in the third quarter and it will take time for the unemployment rate to fall back below 10%, a senior Federal Reserve official said Thursday. (published 2340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BOC'S CARNEY: BASEL GROUP, G20 TO ADOPT CANADA-STYLE BANK REGS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Basic leverage caps imposed under the Canadian banking regulations system will form part of international standards to be adopted in coming months, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  Governor Mark Carney said Thursday. (published 0133 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: INDONESIA GRAFT FIGHT HAS UPSIDE FOR INVESTORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The antigraft scandal that has rocked Indonesia may have unnerved some investors, but the drive to clean upthe judiciary stands to benefit markets and the economy in the long run. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: SINGAPORE OCTOBER CPI LIKELY DOWN 0.5% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore likely remained in technical deflation in October due to a higher base from unusually steep prices a year earlier and slower economic activity. (published 0403 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: YEN OPTIONS FLAT; SEEN FALLING ON SUBDUED SPOT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen options were unchanged in Asia Friday, but dealers said prices are likely to fall in the weeks ahead as the underlying exchange rate remains stable. (published 0323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IN THE MONEY: TREASURY GOES DUTCH FOR WARRANT AUCTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For once, the taxpayer is the smart money. Treasury announced Thursday it will soon auction warrants that are likely to fetch a $2 billion profit and test a critical new avenue to sell equity stakes taxpayers hold in more than 300 publicly traded financial institutions. (published 0301 GMT) [ 20-11-09 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091120e5bk000ce\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
